It is not a shot-for-shot remake, but we did use their script as a template, and there
它不是逐个镜头的翻拍，但我们确实以他们的剧本为模板，并且

171
00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.550
are some adjustments.
做了一些调整。

172
00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:52.890
There are elements, though.
不过，确实有一些元素。

173
00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.710
There are elements that are the same that if you watch it and watch this one.
如果你对比着看两部剧，会发现有些元素是一样的。

174
00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:57.830
Yes.
没错。

175
00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:03.550
For example, in general, each of the characters and the fact that there's this buffoonish,
例如，大体上，每个角色以及这样一个事实：英版里有个滑稽、

176
00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:07.890
silly boss in their version named David Brent and ours, Michael Scott.
愚蠢的老板叫大卫·布伦特，而我们的是迈克尔·斯科特。

177
00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:11.430
But if you look at the talking heads, there are some differences.
但如果你看那些面对镜头的访谈片段，就会发现一些不同之处。

178
00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:12.070
Yes.
是的。

179
00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:14.930
And also, like, the way the story is told is a little different.
而且，故事的讲述方式也略有不同。

180
00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:19.550
I mean, some of the points are the same that happened, but it's told differently.
我的意思是，发生的一些点是一样的，但讲述方式不同。

181
00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:25.510
But Greg Daniels was the person who was tasked with Americanizing the British show.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯是负责将这部英剧本土化的人。

182
00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.110
Yes.
没错。

183
00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:30.450
And Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant kind of oversaw that process.
瑞奇·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫昌特算是监督了整个过程。

184
00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:34.130
But they, for example, they were not on set when we were shooting the pilot.
但比如，我们在拍摄试播集时，他们并没有在片场。

185
00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:34.810
Nope.
没有。

186
00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:35.210
No.
没在。

187
00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.190
They came and they visited with us.
他们后来来探过班。

188
00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:41.550
I remember sitting and getting to have lunch with Ricky Gervais.
我记得当时坐下来和瑞奇·热维斯一起吃了午饭。

189
00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:42.170
Yeah.
是啊。

190
00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:43.830
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

191
00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.130
Were you nervous?
你当时紧张吗？

192
00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:45.930
Oh, yes.
噢，紧张。

193
00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.510
I was a super fan of the British version.
我是英版的超级粉丝。

194
00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:48.990
Me, too.
我也是。

195
00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.590
And I had been cast in the pilot.
我当时已经被选入试播集了。

196
00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.850
And they came and they listened to us do a table read.
他们来了，听了我们的剧本围读。

197
00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:59.610
And afterwards, they asked me, John, Rain, Steve, and BJ, and Greg to join them for lunch
之后，他们邀请我、约翰、雷恩、史蒂夫、BJ还有格雷格一起去吃午饭，

198
00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.870
to discuss the show.
讨论这部剧。

199
00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:08.770
So, and I remember thinking, if I get fired tomorrow, at least I got to have lunch with
所以，我记得当时心想，如果我明天就被解雇了，至少我还能和

200
00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.630
Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant.
瑞奇·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫昌特一起吃过午饭。

201
00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.310
At least that happened.
至少那件事发生了。

202
00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:14.970
That was, to me, just huge.
对我来说，那意义重大。

203
00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.030
Was it a fun lunch?
那顿午餐有趣吗？

204
00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:17.150
I was not at that lunch.
我没参加那顿午餐。

205
00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:17.990
I was not invited.
我没被邀请。

206
00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:21.290
It was so much fun, Angela.
那真的很有趣，安吉拉。

207
00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:24.550
And I remember Ricky saying something in that lunch that was really important.
我记得瑞奇在午餐时说了一些非常重要的话。

208
00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:30.510
He said, you know, in England, you can be really, really bad at your job for a long time
他说，你知道，在英国，你可以很长一段时间工作表现非常非常差，

209
00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.810
and you never get fired.
却永远不会被解雇。

210
00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:35.250
He's like, in America, that's going to frustrate people.
他说，在美国，这种情况会让人们感到沮丧。

211
00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.690
So, my one piece of advice is that Michael can be a buffoon.
所以，他给我的建议是，迈克尔可以是个滑稽的小丑。

212
00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:39.530
He can be silly.
他可以很傻。

213
00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:40.530
He can be irritating.
他可以很烦人。

214
00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:46.270
But you should, I suggest, he said that you show glimpses of him actually being a good
但你应该，我是说，他建议你要展现出他其实是个优秀的销售人员的闪光点，

215
00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.890
salesperson and we do that throughout the show.
我们在整部剧中确实也是这么做的。

216
00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:55.270
You see in future episodes that he is actually good at sales.
你在后续剧集中会看到他其实很擅长销售。

217
00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:58.790
And he said, that's going to be an important, I think, piece of the puzzle.
他说，我认为这将是拼图中重要的一块。

218
00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:05.670
And Stephen Merchant said, my piece of advice would be to lean a little bit more into the
斯蒂芬·莫昌特则说，他的建议是多着重刻画一下

219
00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.010
Jim and Pam relationship.
吉姆和帕姆的关系。

220
00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.450
He said, he knew the heart of it.
他说，他知道那是剧集的核心。

221
00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.830
He said, that's really going to be the heart of your show.
他说，那真的会成为你们剧集的核心。

222
00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.690
Because the British version, they did six episodes for their first season.
因为英版第一季只拍了六集。

223
00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:19.370
Six episodes for their second season and one big Christmas special.
第二季也是六集，外加一个大型圣诞特辑。

224
00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:24.270
And they knew that for American television, we were looking to do years.
他们知道对于美国电视市场，我们打算做很多年。

225
00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:26.370
And we ended up doing 200.
最终我们拍了200集。

226
00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.970
So, he said, you need to keep the heart beating on the show.
所以他说，你需要让剧集的核心保持跳动。

227
00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.610
And so, that's the heart of the show.
所以，那就是剧集的核心。

228
00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:33.370
That's Jim and Pam.
那就是吉姆和帕姆。

229
00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:35.050
Okay, I have another fast fact.
好了，我还有一个冷知识。

230
00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:39.630
We filmed the pilot six months before the rest of season one.
我们是在第一季其余部分拍摄前六个月拍的试播集。

231
00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:44.930
And we shot it on the second floor of a real office building in Culver City.
我们在卡尔弗城一栋真实办公楼的二楼拍摄的。

232
00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:47.130
So, it was an actual office building.
所以，那是一栋真正的办公楼。

233
00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:50.050
And a lot of times on sets, they build the office.
通常在片场，他们会搭建办公室场景。

234
00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.570
So, if they want to film and get a certain camera angle, they can move a wall.
这样如果他们想拍摄特定的机位角度，就可以移动墙壁。

235
00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:54.450
They can move a window.
他们可以移动窗户。

236
00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:55.990
They can move a door because they built it.
他们可以移动门，因为那是搭建出来的。

237
00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:58.310
They actually say, wall flying out.
他们甚至会喊“墙壁移开”。

238
00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.550
And they move a whole wall.
然后他们会把整面墙移走。

239
00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:00.490
They move a whole wall.
他们会把整面墙移走。

240
00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:00.930
It's insane.
这太疯狂了。

241
00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:05.110
On our show, because it was in an actual office building, you just had to work with it.
在我们的剧中，因为是在真正的办公楼里，你只能因地制宜。

242
00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:10.010
And it sort of really lended itself to the documentary style that all the shots weren't going to look pretty.
这反而成就了纪录片风格，因为所有的镜头看起来都不会那么完美。

243
00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:14.950
They weren't going to be lined up just right because they had to work around actual walls and windows.
它们不会排列得恰到好处，因为必须绕过真实的墙壁和窗户拍摄。

244
00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.430
They couldn't just pop them out.
他们不能直接把墙拆掉。

245
00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:23.790
I remember speaking to Ken Kwapis, our director, about setting certain rules for the documentary style of filming.
我记得曾和我们的导演肯·卡皮斯讨论过为纪录片拍摄风格设定一些规则。

246
00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:34.790
And he said it was very important to him that for all of the actors and the crew that the set felt like a real working office and a real documentary was happening.
他说对他而言非常重要的一点是，让所有演员和工作人员都觉得片场就是一个真实工作的办公室，感觉就像真的在拍摄纪录片一样。

247
00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:45.130
And so, one of the rules that he came up with was that he cleared the entire set of all crew members except for a camera operator, a boom operator, and himself.
所以，他提出的其中一条规则是，清空整个片场，除了摄影师、收音师和他自己，不留任何工作人员。

248
00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:45.730
Yes.
是的。

249
00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:46.530
And that was it.
仅此而已。

250
00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:47.030
That was it.
仅此而已。

251
00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:53.970
He also made all of the actors come in every morning, go through hair and makeup, and then sit at our desks starting at 7.30 a.m.
他还要求所有演员每天早上都得过来，做完发型和化妆，然后从早上7点半开始坐在办公桌前。

252
00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:55.670
And we had to pretend to work.
我们还得假装在工作。

253
00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:56.670
Yes.
没错。

254
00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:00.530
And he walked around with the documentary crew and filmed us for 30 minutes.
他带着纪录片摄制组四处走动，拍了我们30分钟。

255
00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:02.430
Yeah, just us quietly working.
对，就是拍我们安静工作的样子。

256
00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:10.670
And little shots that you see, for example, of Pam doing whiteout, that is a piece of B-roll from one of those working mornings that we did.
你看到的那些小镜头，比如帕姆用修正液的画面，就是我们在那些工作早晨拍摄的空镜素材。

257
00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:12.350
And we did that every day on the pilot.
试播集拍摄期间，我们每天都这么做。

258
00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:20.250
Something else about this episode that I noticed is that there is a random exterior shot of a building.
关于这一集，我还注意到一件事，就是有一个随机的建筑物外景镜头。

259
00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.930
Oh, Jenna, let me tell you.
噢，珍娜，让我来告诉你。

260
00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:22.570
Well, wait, wait.
等等，等等。

261
00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.170
Let me grab one of my colorful note cards, as you call them.
让我拿一张你所谓的彩色笔记卡出来。

262
00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:29.410
Exterior shot at 9.29, 9 minutes and 29 seconds.
9分29秒处的外景镜头。

263
00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:30.590
Not our building.
那不是我们的办公楼。

264
00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.250
With a huge exclamation point.
后面还加了个巨大的感叹号。

265
00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:32.430
See?
看到了吗？

266
00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.510
This was a big discovery.
这可是个大发现。

267
00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:35.150
This was a big discovery for me.
对我来说是个大发现。

268
00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:40.170
Not only not our building, it wasn't the building we were filming in.
那不仅不是我们的办公楼，甚至都不是我们拍摄时所在的建筑。

269
00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:41.450
I don't know where they got that shot.
我不知道他们从哪弄来的那个镜头。

270
00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:41.890
I don't know.
我不知道。

271
00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:43.370
It's like stock footage from something?
就像是哪里的库存素材？

272
00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.550
I think it was stock footage.
我觉得应该是库存素材。

273
00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:46.330
And then we never use it again.
而且之后我们就再也没用过它。

274
00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:47.450
That was it.
就那一次。

275
00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:48.070
That was it.
就那一次。

276
00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.670
They should go back and take that out.
他们应该回去把它删掉。

277
00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.450
See you later.
回头见。

278
00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:52.730
And put a shot of the reels under Mifflin exterior.
换成邓德米福林公司的外景镜头。

279
00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.330
Jenna's getting sassy on you.
珍娜开始跟你较真了。

280
00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:55.290
Yeah, I'm going to call someone.
没错，我要给谁打个电话。

281
00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.830
Someone get it right.
得有人把它改对。

282
00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:57.710
All right.
好吧。

283
00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:00.670
Here is my last fast fact for this episode.
这是我关于这一集的最后一个快讯。

284
00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:01.450
Okay, lady.
好的，女士。

285
00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.550
Meredith is not Meredith.
梅雷迪思不是梅雷迪思。

286
00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:04.330
She is not.
她确实不是。

287
00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.270
She is Henriette.
她是亨丽埃特。

288
00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:06.210
It's Henriette.
是亨丽埃特。

289
00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:06.810
Yes.
是的。

290
00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:12.750
Meredith is played by Henriette Mantell in the pilot episode, Not Kate Flannery.
试播集里的梅雷迪思是由亨丽埃特·曼特尔饰演的，而不是凯特·弗兰纳里。

291
00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:13.910
This is true.
这是真的。

292
00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:21.110
Henriette Mantell was a comedy actress who had just broken out because she had played Alice in the Brady Bunch filMs.
亨丽埃特·曼特尔是一位喜剧演员，她当时刚崭露头角，因为她在《布雷迪家族》电影中饰演了爱丽丝。

293
00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:23.770
And she was there for the pilot.
她当时参与了试播集的拍摄。

294
00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:27.950
And then it was six months later that we got picked up.
后来过了六个月，我们才正式获得预订。

295
00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.590
And then we started filming the rest of the episodes.
然后我们开始拍摄剩下的剧集。

296
00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:33.310
And I guess the rumor was she was not available.
我猜传闻是她当时没档期。

297
00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:33.950
She was busy.
她很忙。

298
00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:34.990
And we had to recast her.
所以我们不得不重新选角。

299
00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:36.570
And so Kate Flannery came in.
于是凯特·弗兰纳里就来了。

300
00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:37.870
Here is my fast fact.
这是我的快讯。

301
00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.470
Kate Flannery and I met years before the office.
凯特·弗兰纳里和我早在《办公室》之前就认识了。

302
00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:45.830
We were in an all-female improv group called Bitch Planet.
我们当时在一个全女性即兴表演团体，叫“婊子星球”。

303
00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:46.910
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

304
00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:47.970
Aw, Bitch Planet.
噢，“婊子星球”。

305
00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.950
Sunday nights at like 10 p.m.
周日晚上十点左右。

306
00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:50.650
That's when you want to.
那是你最想看的时候。

307
00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.230
It's exactly when you want your comedy.
那正是你最想看喜剧的时候。

308
00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:53.090
That's when you want to watch improv.
那正是你最想看即兴表演的时候。

309
00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:55.190
Kate and I had known each other for a really long time.
凯特和我认识真的很久了。

310
00:11:55.330 --> 00:12:00.210
And also, Oscar Nunez and I did a sketch comedy show together called Hot Towel.
而且，奥斯卡·努内兹和我还一起做过一个叫“热毛巾”的素描喜剧节目。

311
00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:01.970
Where do you get these names, Angela?
安吉拉，你这些名字都是从哪儿想出来的？

312
00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:04.270
So it was really fun for me because here I am.
所以对我来说真的很有趣，因为我就在那儿。

313
00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.350
Like, I was so nervous the first day.
第一天的时候我特别紧张。

314
00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.270
I didn't know Oscar had been caSt.
我不知道奥斯卡也被选上了。

315
00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:09.630
He didn't know I had been caSt.
他也不知道我被选上了。

316
00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.170
You guys, this was sort of before.
伙计们，那是在那之前的事儿了。

317
00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.530
This was before smartphones.
那是在智能手机出现之前。

318
00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:17.290
Like, it's not like you, like, texted someone you got a role or you put it on your social media.
不像现在，你得到一个角色会发短信告诉别人，或者发到社交媒体上。

319
00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:18.630
There was none of that.
那时候根本没有这些。

320
00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.950
So you walked in and were completely surprised.
所以你走进去的时候会感到非常惊喜。

321
00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.030
I was completely surprised when I saw Oscar.
当我看到奥斯卡时，我真的非常惊喜。

322
00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:28.190
And not only did I see Oscar, but Ken Coapa sat us next to each other.
而且不仅看到了奥斯卡，肯·夸皮还让我们坐在一起。

323
00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:30.250
So I was like, oh my God, I'm going to be okay.
所以我当时就想，天哪，我会没事的。

324
00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:31.270
That's amazing.
太棒了。

325
00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:32.230
My buddy's here.
我的好哥们儿在这儿。

326
00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.930
And then Brian walked in as Kevin and I was like, here we go.
然后布莱恩作为凯文走进来，我就想，我们要开始了。

327
00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:35.810
We're off to the races.
我们要大干一场了。

328
00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:37.650
You guys were amazing in accounting.
你们在会计部表现得太棒了。

329
00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:38.650
Thank you.
谢谢。

330
00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:39.810
Yeah, thank you so much.
是啊，太感谢了。

331
00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:41.030
I'm giving you a compliment.
我是在夸你们呢。

332
00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:41.530
Thank you so much.
真的非常感谢。

333
00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:46.050
So yeah, so I was so excited to have these friends that I had performed with for years
所以，能有这些我在《办公室》之前就已经合作表演多年的朋友

334
00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.450
before the office sitting in my little corner back there.
坐在我后面的小角落里，我真的太兴奋了。

335
00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.450
I remember meeting everyone for the first time.
我记得第一次见到大家的情景。

336
00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.210
Do you remember your first impressions of people?
你还记得对大家的第一印象吗？

337
00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:54.150
I do.
记得。

338
00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.890
I remember my first impression of Rainn Wilson.
我记得我对雷恩·威尔森的第一印象。

339
00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:56.690
Tell me.
快告诉我。

340
00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:00.810
Well, I met Rainn Wilson at a live test audition.
嗯，我是在一次现场试镜中见到雷恩·威尔森的。

341
00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:05.770
So for all the leads of the show, they brought us into screen test and they mixed and matched
当时剧组把所有主角都叫去进行试镜，然后把我们

342
00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:06.050
us.
混搭在一起。

343
00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:09.490
There were four Pams and four Dwights and four Jims and four Michaels.
当时有四个帕姆、四个德怀特、四个吉姆和四个迈克尔。

344
00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:12.730
And we spent an entire day being mixed and matched with each other.
我们花了一整天时间互相搭戏。

345
00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:18.510
And I remember I met Rainn Wilson and he was in character, but I couldn't really know
我记得我见到雷恩·威尔森时，他当时正处于角色状态，但我当时并不知道

346
00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:21.070
that because I didn't know Rainn yet.
因为我还不了解雷恩。

347
00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:25.930
And I thought he was the weirdest person I'd ever met in my life.
我当时觉得他是我这辈子见过最奇怪的人。

348
00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.550
Wait, he was in character the whole time?
等等，他全程都在角色状态里？

349
00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:27.930
Yeah.
是的。

350
00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.270
He just was Dwight.
他当时就是德怀特。

351
00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:30.710
Oh, so method, Rainn.
噢，真是太入戏了，雷恩。

352
00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:31.530
He was in character like that.
他当时就是那样沉浸在角色里的。

353
00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:32.710
So method.
太入戏了。

354
00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:33.490
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

355
00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:35.170
I kind of did the same thing.
我其实也做了同样的事。

356
00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.930
I did my Pam hairstyle.
我弄了帕姆的发型。

357
00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:42.870
The hairstyle that I wore on the show, I sort of invented through the audition process.
我在剧中留的那种发型，其实是我在试镜过程中琢磨出来的。

358
00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:43.070
Right.
没错。

359
00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:47.410
That sort of half up, half down, scrunchy, air-dried curl.
就是那种半扎发、用发圈扎着、自然风干的卷发。

360
00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:49.810
And so I was very quiet.
所以我当时非常安静。

361
00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:54.750
I didn't talk to people in the waiting room because I just thought Pam was sort of not a
我在候场室里没跟人说话，因为我觉得帕姆不是那种

362
00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.850
chatter and I didn't want to get out of character.
爱聊天的人，我不想出戏。

363
00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:58.690
I remember one of the first things.
我记得其中一件最早的事。

364
00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:01.790
Wait, this is so random, but it's true.
等等，这事儿很随机，但却是真的。

365
00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:06.030
That first week of filming, Rainn's wife came to have lunch.
拍摄的第一周，雷恩的妻子来探班吃午饭。

366
00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:12.050
And this is the main interaction I remember from Rainn during the pilot episode.
这是我在试播集期间对雷恩印象最深的一次互动。

367
00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:14.710
Rainn introduced me to his wife.
雷恩把我介绍给了他妻子。

368
00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.010
She was pregnant at the time with their son.
她当时正怀着他们的儿子。

369
00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:17.450
Yes.
是的。

370
00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:21.130
And he said, this is my wife, Holly, bearer of my seed.
他说，这是我妻子霍莉，我骨肉的承载者。

371
00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:26.900
And she started laughing.
她当时就笑了起来。

372
00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:29.080
But that was just Rain being Rain.
但那就是雷恩，一贯的雷恩。

373
00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:29.540
That's Rain.
那就是雷恩。

374
00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:30.320
That is Rain.
确实是雷恩。

375
00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:31.620
But wouldn't Dwight say that?
但德怀特不也会这么说吗？

376
00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:32.900
He would also say that.
他也会这么说的。

377
00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.100
This is Angela, bearer of my seed.
这是安吉拉，我骨肉的承载者。

378
00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:34.620
Yes.
没错。

379
00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:35.640
It's amazing how...
真神奇，怎么……

380
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.800
She's carrying my seed.
她怀着我的骨肉。

381
00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.080
I'm like, oh my God.
我当时心想，天哪。

382
00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:41.820
I feel like we all had little parts of our characters in us.
我觉得我们每个人身上都有角色的一小部分。

383
00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:45.540
But I don't know if that's true of you because you are so opposite from Angela Martin.
但我不知道这对你是否适用，因为你和安吉拉·马丁完全是两类人。

384
00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:46.060
I am.
确实如此。

385
00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:52.160
I was thinking about how you were saying, like, you stayed in character and so did Rainn in between your auditions in the lobby.
我刚才在想你说的，你和雷恩在试镜间隙都保持着角色状态。

386
00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:53.340
I would not have.
我就做不到。

387
00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:59.540
I would have been like, chitty-chat-chat, chitty-chat-chat, and then I would have just turned into a bitch when I entered the room.
我会一直在那儿叽叽喳喳聊个不停，然后一进房间再瞬间变脸成个刻薄鬼。

388
00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:04.700
Well, you know, I didn't have any scenes with Rainn in the pilot of Substance.
嗯，你知道，在试播集里我和雷恩没有对手戏。

389
00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:05.940
I didn't have any one-on-one scenes.
我没有和他单独的戏份。

390
00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:15.060
So for me, when we were shooting the pilot, the people that I really bonded with were Steve, John, and you because you were over the little part.
所以对我来说，拍试播集时，我真正建立起感情的是史蒂夫、约翰和你，因为你就坐在隔壁。

391
00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.520
You were my closest seatmate in the office.
你在办公室里是我最近的邻座。

392
00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:18.960
So you and I bonded.
所以我们俩建立了感情。

393
00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:28.240
And I remember after we finished the pilot and we all left and we didn't know if we were going to be picked up or make any more, shortly after that, I turned 30 years old.
我记得拍完试播集后，我们都离开了，不知道剧集会不会被续订，也不知道以后还会不会再拍，就在那之后不久，我满30岁了。

394
00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.420
It was a big milestone birthday for me.
那对我来说是一个重要的里程碑生日。

395
00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:34.280
And I really wondered if I should invite any of you guys.
我当时真的很纠结要不要邀请你们。

396
00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:35.800
And I didn't.
结果我没邀请。

397
00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:40.420
I didn't invite you guys because I thought, well, I'm probably never going to see them again.
我没邀请你们，因为我想，反正我可能再也见不到你们了。

398
00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:44.160
Should I throw you another 30th birthday party and invite everyone?
要不我再为你办一次30岁生日派对，把大家都请来？

399
00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:45.340
Would you?
你会吗？

400
00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:47.760
And then we could just say happy 30th.
然后我们就能说声30岁生日快乐了。

401
00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:48.660
Will you?
你会吗？

402
00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:49.700
Okay.
好吧。

403
00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:55.400
Because now you guys are some of my closest friends and you aren't at my milestone birthday.
因为现在你们是我最亲密的朋友，却没能参加我的里程碑式生日派对。

404
00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:55.860
Aw.
噢。

405
00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:58.600
Okay, we'll have to throw you a 30th birthday party.
好吧，我们得为你补办一个30岁生日派对。

406
00:15:58.760 --> 00:15:59.500
It won't be weird.
不会尴尬的。

407
00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:00.700
All right, guys.
好了，各位。

408
00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:04.160
So next up, we are going to break down this episode.
接下来，我们要深入剖析这一集。

409
00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:05.820
We're going to really get into the nitty gritty.
我们要深入探讨细节。

410
00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:08.260
We're going to talk about scenes and memories and stories.
我们要聊聊剧中的场景、回忆和故事。

411
00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:09.100
So stick with us.
所以请继续收听。

412
00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.200
We're talking about the pilot episode of The Office.
我们要聊的是《办公室》的第一集。

413
00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:18.220
And I think we should talk about some of our favorite moments, Jenna.
我觉得我们应该聊聊我们最喜欢的片段，珍娜。

414
00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:18.820
Yes.
没错。

415
00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:23.040
Well, one of my favorite moments is the dynamic between Pam and Michael.
嗯，我最喜欢的片段之一是帕姆和迈克尔之间的互动。

416
00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.300
I mean, selfishly, I guess I'm in that moment.
我是说，自私点讲，我正好也在那个片段里。

417
00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:25.660
Yeah.
是啊。

418
00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:28.220
But I really loved working with Steve Carell.
但我真的很喜欢和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔合作。

419
00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:33.020
I really loved how much he let me be silent and just look at him.
我特别喜欢他给了我很多沉默的空间，让我只是看着他。

420
00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:33.880
And just react.
只是做出反应。

421
00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:34.400
Yes.
没错。

422
00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.220
I loved that.
我喜欢那样。

423
00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:41.260
But I especially love whenever Melora Hardin, who plays Jan Levinson Gould, got in the mix.
但我尤其喜欢梅罗拉·哈丁饰演的简·莱文森·古尔德加入进来的那些时刻。

424
00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:42.560
She's so commanding.
她非常有威严。

425
00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:45.780
Just like Melora's presence is like, I'm scared of her.
梅罗拉的气场就是那种让我感到害怕的类型。

426
00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:46.240
Yes.
是的。

427
00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:46.880
I get it.
我懂。

428
00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.880
I get why he was a little scared of her.
我明白为什么他会有点怕她了。

429
00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:56.100
And I love the scene where Michael tries to throw Pam under the bus about why he doesn't have the agenda that he's supposed to have.
我特别喜欢迈克尔试图把没带议程的责任推给帕姆的那场戏。

430
00:16:56.220 --> 00:17:02.500
And it's because he told her to throw it in the receptacle, the trash can that is a special filing cabinet for corporate memos.
因为他之前告诉她把议程扔进那个容器里，那个被他称为公司备忘录专用档案柜的垃圾桶。

431
00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:14.360
And I remember shooting that scene, and I just remember every time that Pam said, you told me to put it in a special filing cabinet that is a trash can, that we would giggle.
我记得拍那场戏的时候，每次帕姆说“你让我把它放进那个作为垃圾桶的专用档案柜里”时，我们都会忍不住笑场。

432
00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:21.320
And so I just remember the matter-of-factness of that moment and how fun that was.
所以我记得那个时刻那种一本正经的感觉，真的很有趣。

433
00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:24.420
Pam totally stood up for herself in her own little way in that moment.
帕姆在那一刻以她自己的方式完全捍卫了自己。

434
00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.020
Here's the thing about Steve Carell.
关于史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，情况是这样的。

435
00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.780
He is one of the nicest people you will ever meet.
他是我见过最友善的人之一。

436
00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.200
He is so nice.
他真的太好了。

437
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:35.060
I know it's almost even become like a joke, like Steve Carell's the nicest person ever, but he is.
我知道这几乎都快成了一个梗，大家都说史蒂夫·卡瑞尔是史上最友善的人，但他确实如此。

438
00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:35.460
I know.
我知道。

439
00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.100
And people ask me a lot, what's it like to work with Steve Carell?
人们经常问我，和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔一起工作是什么感觉？

440
00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:39.820
Are you just laughing all the time?
你们是不是一直在笑？

441
00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:44.220
And no, you're not laughing all the time because Steve isn't on all the time.
不，并不是一直在笑，因为史蒂夫不会时刻都在表演。

442
00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:45.180
He's not one of those.
他不是那种人。

443
00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:45.660
He's a real person.
他是个真实的人。

444
00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:46.520
He's a real person.
他是个真实的人。

445
00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:50.160
And he's, he's, I've worked with comedians who are on all the time.
而且，我曾和那些时刻都在表演的喜剧演员合作过。

446
00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:54.380
You walk around and you can just, they can't turn off their joke-making brain.
你走在他们身边，能感觉到他们的大脑根本停不下来，一直在想段子。

447
00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.280
I drive my cursor.
我开着我的车。

448
00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:56.560
It's a little insane.
这有点疯狂。

449
00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:58.140
Steve is not like that.
史蒂夫不是那样的人。

450
00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:03.200
But you and Steve and I would sit and have long conversations about the best frozen
但你、史蒂夫和我曾经坐在一起，长谈过关于最好的冷冻

451
00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.780
yogurt in the San Fernando Valley.
圣费尔南多谷的酸奶。

452
00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:09.960
Oh, I will never forget the morning, on Monday mornings, Steve would come out of his office,
噢，我永远忘不了那个早晨，在周一的早上，史蒂夫会从他的办公室走出来，

453
00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.240
out of Michael Scott's office between scenes.
在拍摄间隙从迈克尔·斯科特的办公室出来。

454
00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.540
He would walk over to Jenna and I, and we would talk about our weekends.
他会走到我和珍娜身边，我们会聊起各自的周末。

455
00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.980
And one Monday morning, he walked over and he was like, ladies, guess what I did this weekend?
有一个周一早上，他走过来，就像是说，女士们，猜猜我这个周末干了什么？

456
00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:20.460
We're like, what?
我们问，干了什么？

457
00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:21.680
And he goes, I went to Target.
他说，我去了塔吉特百货。

458
00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:21.800
Target.
塔吉特。

459
00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:23.700
He would talk to us about Target.
他会跟我们聊塔吉特。

460
00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.340
And he told us about his Target run.
他跟我们讲了他去塔吉特购物的事。

461
00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.380
It was really, really sweet.
那真的、真的非常可爱。

462
00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:33.800
You know, recently, I was in a Michaels purchasing some supplies for a crafting job.
你知道，最近，我在一家迈克尔斯手工店买些做手工用的材料。

463
00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:39.240
And the checkout guy said, oh my gosh, now this is getting crazy.
收银员说，天哪，这真是太疯狂了。

464
00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.060
This morning, Oscar Nunez came in here.
今天早上，奥斯卡·努涅斯刚来过这儿。

465
00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.480
Then Steve Carell.
然后是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

466
00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:44.280
And now you?
现在又是你？

467
00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:45.680
