So, in the background, there are two women, and they are the real production company accountants for our show.
在背景里，有两个女人，她们是我们剧组真正的制作公司会计。

630
00:24:37.700 --> 00:24:43.800
Yes, we needed more people to fill out the space, and they pulled in our actual accountants from our production office.
是的，我们需要更多人来填满空间，于是他们把我们制作办公室里真正的会计拉了过来。

631
00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:48.960
Yes, Ken Guapas, the director, walked into the production office and asked if anyone would like to be in the background of a scene.
没错，导演肯·瓜帕斯走进制作办公室，问有没有人想在背景里客串一下。

632
00:24:49.100 --> 00:24:52.160
And those two women came and sat there for that couple of hours.
那两个女人就来了，在那里坐了几个小时。

633
00:24:52.400 --> 00:24:53.460
They were so giddy.
她们当时特别兴奋。

634
00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:54.600
They loved it.
她们很喜欢。

635
00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:55.240
They loved it.
她们很喜欢。

636
00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:55.740
They loved it.
她们很喜欢。

637
00:24:55.840 --> 00:25:03.200
And then, also, in the conference room, some faces you might see sprinkled through the first season, but then they don't go past that season, are Luann Kelly,
另外，在会议室里，你可能会在第一季中零星看到一些面孔，但之后她们就没再出现过了，比如卢安·凯利，

638
00:25:03.440 --> 00:25:04.840
who worked in the annex.
她在附楼工作。

639
00:25:05.180 --> 00:25:05.340
Yes.
没错。

640
00:25:05.340 --> 00:25:06.540
She is someone that you see a lot.
她是那种你经常能看到的人。

641
00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:09.220
I get asked a lot, who is the lady in the annex?
经常有人问我，附楼里的那个女士是谁？

642
00:25:09.400 --> 00:25:09.600
Yes.
是的。

643
00:25:09.640 --> 00:25:10.020
It's Luann.
那是卢安。

644
00:25:10.020 --> 00:25:13.080
She was sort of over where Mindy ends up sitting.
她当时坐在明迪后来坐的位置附近。

645
00:25:13.380 --> 00:25:13.540
Yes.
没错。

646
00:25:13.620 --> 00:25:14.440
By Kelly's desk.
在凯利的办公桌旁边。

647
00:25:14.580 --> 00:25:20.080
And then, also, of course, Devin and Creed, who ultimately do have a storyline that will come later.
还有，当然，德文和克里德，他们最终确实会有后续的剧情。

648
00:25:20.080 --> 00:25:20.940
But not until season two.
但要等到第二季。

649
00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:21.560
That's right.
没错。

650
00:25:21.560 --> 00:25:26.180
So, for an entire season, you just see Devin and Creed in the background of scenes.
所以，整整一季，你只能在背景里看到德文和克里德。

651
00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:28.300
They don't get any lines until the second season.
直到第二季他们才有台词。

652
00:25:28.340 --> 00:25:32.120
But that is the only scene our actual accountants are in, because then they had to go back to work.
但那是我们真正的会计师出镜的唯一一场戏，因为之后他们就得回去工作了。

653
00:25:32.260 --> 00:25:32.640
They did.
确实如此。

654
00:25:32.840 --> 00:25:35.120
They had to actually go back to being accountants for the show.
他们真的得回去做节目的会计师了。

655
00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:36.900
I think this is an interesting tidbit.
我觉得这是一个有趣的细节。

656
00:25:37.240 --> 00:25:43.980
Phyllis Smith, who plays Phyllis on the show, she was the casting associate for The Office.
在剧中饰演菲利斯的菲利斯·史密斯，她曾是《办公室》的选角助理。

657
00:25:43.980 --> 00:25:49.060
So, when I auditioned for The Office, she read my audition scenes with me.
所以，当我为《办公室》试镜时，是她和我对戏。

658
00:25:49.440 --> 00:25:51.660
Everyone, I read my scene with Phyllis.
各位，我是和菲利斯对的戏。

659
00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:52.980
That's who I read my scene with.
就是和她对的戏。

660
00:25:53.100 --> 00:25:53.400
Yes.
没错。

661
00:25:53.580 --> 00:25:58.220
And Ken Kwap, as the director, was so taken with how she did her readings with the actors.
而导演肯·卡皮斯对她与演员对戏的方式印象非常深刻。

662
00:25:58.420 --> 00:25:59.640
She's so earnest, you guys.
伙计们，她真的非常真诚。

663
00:25:59.740 --> 00:26:00.900
She is so earneSt.
她太真诚了。

664
00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:04.560
And so real, that he said to Greg Daniels, I want her on the show.
而且非常真实，所以他跟格雷格·丹尼尔斯说，我想让她演这部剧。

665
00:26:05.060 --> 00:26:06.840
Can I give her a part on the show?
我能给她安排个角色吗？

666
00:26:07.260 --> 00:26:14.540
And so, Phyllis went from being a casting associate, which she had done for years with Allison Jones, the casting director.
于是，菲利斯从一名选角助理——她和选角导演艾莉森·琼斯一起做了多年——

667
00:26:14.660 --> 00:26:14.820
Yes.
没错。

668
00:26:14.940 --> 00:26:18.640
Worked with Phyllis, to having a part on this pilot.
和菲利斯一起工作，变成了在这部试播集中拥有一个角色。

669
00:26:18.920 --> 00:26:23.400
And I think because we all thought the show was going nowhere, it was fine.
我想是因为我们当时都觉得这部剧没戏了，所以觉得没关系。

670
00:26:23.420 --> 00:26:26.020
And after the pilot was over, she went back to being a casting associate.
试播集结束后，她又回去做选角助理了。

671
00:26:26.140 --> 00:26:27.060
She went right back to work.
她直接回去工作了。

672
00:26:27.560 --> 00:26:35.300
Phyllis has a great story that she tells that the way she found out that she got Phyllis is that she got sides and they said, Phyllis.
菲利斯有个很棒的故事，她说她发现自己得到菲利斯这个角色是因为她拿到了剧本，上面写着“菲利斯”。

673
00:26:36.240 --> 00:26:38.080
Oh, so there was a character.
哦，所以当时已经有这个角色了。

674
00:26:38.280 --> 00:26:38.440
Yeah.
是的。

675
00:26:38.600 --> 00:26:39.520
And they named it Phyllis.
而且他们直接以她的名字命名。

676
00:26:39.560 --> 00:26:41.140
And Ken was like, that's you.
肯当时就说，那就是你。

677
00:26:41.260 --> 00:26:41.880
You're Phyllis.
你就是菲利斯。

678
00:26:42.020 --> 00:26:42.800
And she was like, what?
她当时就懵了，什么？

679
00:26:43.720 --> 00:26:47.520
We wrote a part for you based on the numerous readings with actors.
我们根据你和演员们无数次的对戏，为你写了一个角色。

680
00:26:47.740 --> 00:26:49.140
You're now in the show, Phyllis.
菲利斯，你现在是剧组的一员了。

681
00:26:49.240 --> 00:26:53.900
Which is just so cool because Phyllis had wanted to be an actress.
这真的太酷了，因为菲利斯一直想当演员。

682
00:26:54.200 --> 00:26:54.980
She had been an actress.
她以前当过演员。

683
00:26:55.140 --> 00:26:56.220
She had been a burlesque dancer.
她还当过滑稽舞演员。

684
00:26:56.220 --> 00:26:56.700
Burlesque dancer.
滑稽舞演员。

685
00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:57.980
No one can shimmy.
没人能像她那样扭动身体。

686
00:26:58.120 --> 00:26:59.540
No one can shimmy like Phyllis.
没人能像菲利斯那样扭动。

687
00:26:59.780 --> 00:27:00.080
That's right.
没错。

688
00:27:00.100 --> 00:27:01.160
She has a great shimmy.
她扭得特别棒。

689
00:27:01.320 --> 00:27:08.360
She had an amazing photo on her desk because Ken Kwapis wanted us to personalize our desk for the pilot episode and moving forward.
她的桌上有一张很棒的照片，因为肯·卡皮斯希望我们在试播集及后续拍摄中个性化布置自己的办公桌。

690
00:27:08.560 --> 00:27:10.340
So we all brought in something from home.
所以我们都从家里带了些东西来。

691
00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:15.880
I have a photo of myself and my grandmother and a frame that says, I heart grandma.
我带了一张我和祖母的照片，相框上写着“我爱祖母”。

692
00:27:16.200 --> 00:27:20.260
And my eyes are closed in the photo, but my grandmother framed it anyway.
照片里我闭着眼睛，但祖母还是把它装裱了起来。

693
00:27:21.240 --> 00:27:26.200
And so I have that on my desk and it just kind of like tickled me and made me think of my grandmother.
所以我把它放在桌上，这让我觉得很有趣，也让我想起了祖母。

694
00:27:26.560 --> 00:27:29.160
I had a picture of me and my sister swimming in Lake of the Ozarks.
我带了一张我和姐姐在欧扎克湖游泳的照片。

695
00:27:29.340 --> 00:27:29.680
Yes.
是的。

696
00:27:29.800 --> 00:27:37.420
And Phyllis had a picture of herself in her full burlesque outfit with a red feather boa draped over her shoulders.
而菲利斯带了一张她穿着全套滑稽舞服装的照片，肩上披着一条红色羽毛围巾。

697
00:27:37.820 --> 00:27:39.140
Angela, let's take a quick break.
安吉拉，我们休息一下吧。

698
00:27:39.380 --> 00:27:39.940
Okay, Jenna.
好的，珍娜。

699
00:27:40.480 --> 00:27:41.500
You're going to get a snack.
你要去吃点零食吗？

700
00:27:41.900 --> 00:27:42.280
Why?
为什么？

701
00:27:42.960 --> 00:27:45.140
Because you always get a snack during the breaks.
因为你总是在休息时间去吃零食。

702
00:27:45.360 --> 00:27:45.680
I do.
我确实会。

703
00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:53.320
So then we get to that crazy scene where Michael is walking Ryan the temp around.
然后我们就看到了那场疯狂的戏，迈克尔带着临时工瑞安到处转。

704
00:27:53.320 --> 00:27:56.660
So he's just been told that we need downsizing.
当时他刚被告知我们需要裁员。

705
00:27:56.880 --> 00:27:58.440
And then he hires a temp.
结果他却雇了个临时工。

706
00:27:59.480 --> 00:28:00.600
He hires them.
他雇了他们。

707
00:28:00.680 --> 00:28:02.240
It's the opposite of downsizing.
这和裁员完全相反。

708
00:28:02.260 --> 00:28:02.920
It's the opposite.
完全相反。

709
00:28:03.180 --> 00:28:08.940
Can I just say one thing I love too is when Dwight has his talking head and he said, I've been talking about downsizing for years.
我能说一件我也很喜欢的事吗，就是德怀特在面对镜头采访时说，我谈论裁员已经好几年了。

710
00:28:09.060 --> 00:28:10.180
I brought it up in my interview.
我在面试时就提过这事。

711
00:28:11.080 --> 00:28:12.440
Like, who does that?
天哪，谁会那样做？

712
00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:15.840
He was like interviewing for a job and is like, you should downsize.
他就像是在面试一份工作，然后说，你们应该裁员。

713
00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:17.840
I would like this job.
我想得到这份工作。

714
00:28:17.840 --> 00:28:19.860
I suggest you get rid of three other people.
我建议你们裁掉其他三个人。

715
00:28:20.360 --> 00:28:22.320
So here's a little fun fact.
这里有个有趣的小事实。

716
00:28:22.420 --> 00:28:23.760
It's not a fast fact.
这不是个快速事实。

717
00:28:23.880 --> 00:28:27.920
But a fun fact is that BJ Novak was the first person cast on the show.
但一个有趣的事实是，B.J. 诺瓦克是这部剧第一个定下的演员。

718
00:28:28.560 --> 00:28:29.340
He was?
真的吗？

719
00:28:29.480 --> 00:28:29.900
He was.
是的。

720
00:28:30.200 --> 00:28:32.200
Greg Daniels saw him doing stand-up comedy.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯看过他的单口喜剧表演。

721
00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:35.040
And he thought he was like, this guy.
他当时就觉得，就是这个人。

722
00:28:35.340 --> 00:28:36.480
I want this guy.
我就要这个人。

723
00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:43.800
And so he offered BJ a role as both a writer and the role of Ryan the Temp on the show.
于是他邀请 B.J. 同时担任编剧和剧中临时工瑞安的角色。

724
00:28:43.980 --> 00:28:47.980
So when I came in for my audition, BJ was already caSt.
所以当我来试镜的时候，B.J. 已经定下来了。

725
00:28:48.180 --> 00:28:49.400
He was the very first person.
他是第一个被选中的人。

726
00:28:49.400 --> 00:28:56.140
And he was also the first example of that synergy of having people who were both performers and writers for the show.
他也是这种协同效应的第一个例子，即让既是表演者又是编剧的人参与这部剧。

727
00:28:56.240 --> 00:28:57.440
Which was so great.
这真的很棒。

728
00:28:57.540 --> 00:29:01.760
Something that we haven't talked about, but we will talk about it many times as the show goes,
我们还没谈过，但随着剧集的推进，我们会多次谈到这一点，

729
00:29:01.760 --> 00:29:06.420
is that what a wonderful creative collaboration we had between the writers and the actors.
那就是编剧和演员之间有着多么美妙的创意合作。

730
00:29:06.660 --> 00:29:08.100
And that was because of Greg Daniels.
这都要归功于格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

731
00:29:08.180 --> 00:29:11.520
He sort of set the tone that he wanted this creative collaboration.
他奠定了基调，他想要这种创意合作。

732
00:29:11.520 --> 00:29:12.980
He wanted to hear our ideas.
他想听听我们的想法。

733
00:29:13.160 --> 00:29:14.760
And he wanted writers on the set.
他希望编剧们能出现在片场。

734
00:29:14.920 --> 00:29:18.000
And I think we were just so much the better for it.
我觉得我们因此受益匪浅。

735
00:29:18.140 --> 00:29:21.680
I've been on other shows now where the writers and the actors are separate.
我现在参与过其他剧集，那里的编剧和演员是分开的。

736
00:29:21.680 --> 00:29:22.840
And there's not a lot of collaboration.
没什么合作可言。

737
00:29:23.420 --> 00:29:26.900
It feels weird after having experienced something else.
在体验过那种合作模式后，再经历这些会觉得很奇怪。

738
00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:30.620
No, Greg really trusted us to be the experts of our characters.
没错，格雷格真的很信任我们，让我们成为自己角色的专家。

739
00:29:30.620 --> 00:29:35.380
So whenever he was trying to mull something over or justify something,
所以每当他试图斟酌某事或证明某事合理时，

740
00:29:35.740 --> 00:29:37.480
he would come to us and ask us.
他都会来问我们。

741
00:29:37.580 --> 00:29:39.800
Just in the way that he went to Steve and said,
就像他去找史蒂夫说的那样，

742
00:29:40.120 --> 00:29:43.260
hey, do you have any thoughts on who Michael Scott's heroes would be?
嘿，你觉得迈克尔·斯科特的偶像是谁？

743
00:29:43.420 --> 00:29:43.620
Yeah.
没错。

744
00:29:43.680 --> 00:29:48.080
He trusted us to have done our homework and know our characters so well that we could contribute.
他信任我们已经做好了功课，对自己的角色了如指掌，能够做出贡献。

745
00:29:48.400 --> 00:29:49.160
Yeah, it was great.
是的，那太棒了。

746
00:29:49.240 --> 00:29:49.960
It was really special.
那真的很特别。

747
00:29:50.760 --> 00:29:54.700
So also in that scene, that is the famous stapler in Jell-O.
在那场戏里，还有著名的果冻订书机。

748
00:29:55.080 --> 00:29:55.340
Yeah.
没错。

749
00:29:55.680 --> 00:29:56.680
The stapler goes in Jell-O.
订书机被放进了果冻里。

750
00:29:56.920 --> 00:29:59.240
I have seen so many people recreate this.
我见过好多人重现这一幕。

751
00:29:59.700 --> 00:30:00.140
How?
怎么做到的？

752
00:30:00.140 --> 00:30:00.600
How?
怎么做到的？

753
00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:01.700
I am blown away.
我惊呆了。

754
00:30:01.880 --> 00:30:06.460
Every time I see a fan tag me in a photo where they put something in Jell-O, I'm like,
每次看到粉丝在照片里艾特我，里面放着被果冻包裹的东西时，我都会想，

755
00:30:06.620 --> 00:30:07.380
I'm very impressed.
我印象非常深刻。

756
00:30:07.460 --> 00:30:08.220
Where to go?
去哪儿？

757
00:30:08.420 --> 00:30:08.780
I know.
我知道。

758
00:30:09.060 --> 00:30:12.980
Something we haven't mentioned is the flirtation between Jim and Pam in this episode.
我们还没提到的一点是，这一集中吉姆和帕姆之间的调情。

759
00:30:13.340 --> 00:30:20.400
And it goes on through the whole first two-thirds of this episode or three-quarters of this episode.
这种调情贯穿了这一集的前三分之二甚至四分之三。

760
00:30:20.780 --> 00:30:22.080
Little, little things.
一点点，一点点小细节。

761
00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:24.880
What did I write on my pink note card, Jenna?
我在粉色卡片上写了什么，珍娜？

762
00:30:25.120 --> 00:30:26.000
Mixed berries.
混合浆果。

763
00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:26.880
In quotes.
加引号的。

764
00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:28.280
He's on to me.
他发现我的小秘密了。

765
00:30:28.280 --> 00:30:28.720
Yeah.
是啊。

766
00:30:29.060 --> 00:30:30.560
That is one of the cutest things.
那真是最可爱的事情之一。

767
00:30:30.720 --> 00:30:31.860
It is so pure.
太纯真了。

768
00:30:32.080 --> 00:30:32.480
It is.
确实。

769
00:30:32.480 --> 00:30:36.400
It's like, that's flirting for them that he knows your favorite yogurt.
就像是，他知道你最喜欢的酸奶，这就是他们之间的调情方式。

770
00:30:36.980 --> 00:30:43.320
But up until the end, you are just sort of following this flirtation between the two characters.
但在最后之前，你只是在关注这两个角色之间的调情。

771
00:30:43.320 --> 00:30:46.660
And then all of a sudden, Roy walks in the door.
然后突然间，罗伊走进了门。

772
00:30:46.980 --> 00:30:47.940
David Dinman.
大卫·丁曼。

773
00:30:48.080 --> 00:30:49.560
Carrying that weird trash bag.
提着那个奇怪的垃圾袋。

774
00:30:49.680 --> 00:30:51.300
We never know what's in that trash bag.
我们永远不知道那个垃圾袋里装的是什么。

775
00:30:51.460 --> 00:30:52.300
What is he carrying?
他提着什么呢？

776
00:30:52.300 --> 00:30:56.160
I loved it so much when John and Jim is like, what's in the bag?
我特别喜欢约翰和吉姆问“袋子里装的是什么”的那一段。

777
00:30:56.360 --> 00:30:57.580
Roy's like, yeah, just tell her.
罗伊说，是啊，告诉她吧。

778
00:30:57.740 --> 00:30:59.080
Yeah, tell her I'll meet her in the car.
是啊，告诉她我会在车里等她。

779
00:30:59.240 --> 00:30:59.360
Yeah.
是啊。

780
00:30:59.820 --> 00:31:06.960
But I think it is such a, I remember watching the pilot with people and having them be shocked.
但我认为这真的很……我记得和别人一起看试播集时，他们都感到很震惊。

781
00:31:07.360 --> 00:31:07.760
Yeah.
是啊。

782
00:31:07.960 --> 00:31:08.680
By like, oh, wait.
就像是，哦，等等。

783
00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:09.200
Oh, crap.
天哪。

784
00:31:09.200 --> 00:31:10.900
She's been engaged three years?
她已经订婚三年了？

785
00:31:10.980 --> 00:31:11.440
Three years.
三年了。

786
00:31:11.580 --> 00:31:12.340
Holy moly.
天呐。

787
00:31:12.740 --> 00:31:12.940
Yeah.
是啊。

788
00:31:12.940 --> 00:31:15.240
And then Jim has that heartbreaking talking head.
然后吉姆有了那个令人心碎的采访镜头。

789
00:31:15.360 --> 00:31:17.180
Do I think I'll be invited to the wedding?
我想我会收到婚礼邀请吗？

790
00:31:18.020 --> 00:31:19.140
Oh, Jim.
哦，吉姆。

791
00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:20.760
Breaking hearts.
真是让人心碎。

792
00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:21.580
John Krasinski.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基。

793
00:31:21.580 --> 00:31:21.860
He's breaking hearts.
他让人心碎。

794
00:31:21.860 --> 00:31:23.140
Breaking hearts right out of the gate.
从一开始就让人心碎。

795
00:31:23.140 --> 00:31:23.880
He's breaking hearts.
他让人心碎。

796
00:31:23.880 --> 00:31:24.640
He really is.
他确实是。

797
00:31:24.700 --> 00:31:27.460
So another really cute flirty moment between Jim and Pam.
所以，吉姆和帕姆之间还有另一个非常可爱的调情时刻。

798
00:31:27.780 --> 00:31:31.760
After the conference room scene, where we all find out there's going to be downsizing,
在会议室场景之后，我们都知道要裁员了，

799
00:31:31.980 --> 00:31:35.840
the camera cuts to different groups of people talking about downsizing.
镜头切到不同的人群讨论裁员。

800
00:31:36.200 --> 00:31:39.920
But when it cuts to Jim and Pam, we are not talking about downsizing.
但当镜头切到吉姆和帕姆时，我们谈论的不是裁员。

801
00:31:40.280 --> 00:31:40.980
What are you guys talking about?
你们在聊什么呢？

802
00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:44.220
We are talking about your cat party.
我们在聊你的猫咪派对。

803
00:31:44.440 --> 00:31:45.520
Do you remember this?
你还记得这个吗？

804
00:31:45.580 --> 00:31:46.140
I do.
记得。

805
00:31:46.300 --> 00:31:46.820
I do.
记得。

806
00:31:47.120 --> 00:31:51.560
So this is, I feel like this is really significant and kind of goes on the heels of what we were
我觉得这真的很重要，而且紧接着我们之前讨论的

807
00:31:51.560 --> 00:31:54.160
talking about with Greg wanting to collaborate with actors.
关于格雷格想和演员合作的话题。

808
00:31:54.540 --> 00:31:58.220
So Ken said, listen, I'm just going to roll the camera.
所以肯说，听着，我就直接开机拍摄了。

809
00:31:58.520 --> 00:32:00.020
You two just talk to each other.
你们俩就自顾自地聊天。

810
00:32:00.540 --> 00:32:01.580
Don't push it.
别刻意去演。

811
00:32:01.760 --> 00:32:02.620
Just talk.
就正常聊天。

812
00:32:02.820 --> 00:32:04.040
Make each other laugh.
把对方逗笑就行。

813
00:32:04.240 --> 00:32:07.800
And so here's something you should know is that earlier in the scene,
你们应该知道的是，在那场戏之前，

814
00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:10.900
Ken had asked me if I would pass out papers in the background.
肯问我能不能在背景里发传单。

815
00:32:10.980 --> 00:32:11.400
Yeah.
没错。

816
00:32:11.640 --> 00:32:13.360
I only had three lines in the episode.
我在那一集里只有三句台词。

817
00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:18.160
They were, you know, otherwise I was just background basically for that, you know, pilot.
除此之外，在那一集试播集里，我基本上就是个背景板。

818
00:32:18.560 --> 00:32:24.540
So he asked me if I would pass out papers and I had just doodled a little drawing of a cat
所以他让我发传单，而我当时正好随手画了一只小猫，

819
00:32:24.540 --> 00:32:27.240
and I said, you're invited to Sprinkle's birthday party.
我说，你被邀请参加斯普林克尔的生日派对了。

820
00:32:27.460 --> 00:32:30.900
I just sort of made up that my character had found a cat in the parking lot.
我只是随口编了个故事，说我的角色在停车场捡到了一只猫。

821
00:32:31.040 --> 00:32:31.260
I don't know.
我也不知道。

822
00:32:31.300 --> 00:32:32.480
I was just sort of bored and-
我当时就是有点无聊，然后——

823
00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:33.860
We all made up backstories for ourselves.
我们都为自己的角色编了背景故事。

824
00:32:33.860 --> 00:32:38.800
No, I just made up backstory that my character had found this cat in the parking lot.
不，我只是编了个背景故事，说我的角色在停车场捡到了这只猫。

825
00:32:38.860 --> 00:32:44.080
But I think it's really significant because you in your character actory prep work decided
但我认为这真的很重要，因为你在做角色准备工作时，

826
00:32:44.080 --> 00:32:46.280
that your character was a crazy cat lady.
决定了你的角色是个疯狂的爱猫女士。

827
00:32:46.440 --> 00:32:47.360
I guess I did.
我想确实是这样。

828
00:32:47.500 --> 00:32:50.300
Because you kind of decorated your desk with cat stuff.
因为你用猫咪周边装饰了你的办公桌。

829
00:32:50.300 --> 00:32:56.940
Now, the prop department that set my desk had a paperclip holder that was a cat laying on its side
其实，负责布置我桌子的道具组放了一个回形针盒，那是一只侧卧的猫，

830
00:32:56.940 --> 00:32:58.040
and it holds paperclips.
用来装回形针的。

831
00:32:58.160 --> 00:32:58.360
Okay.
好吧。

832
00:32:58.520 --> 00:32:59.340
I took it from my desk.
我把它从桌子上拿走了。

833
00:32:59.340 --> 00:32:59.960
I still have it.
我现在还留着它。

834
00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:02.840
But I might have stolen it as a memento.
我可能是把它当成纪念品偷走了。

835
00:33:03.020 --> 00:33:05.640
And so I think I was just looking at that and I was doodling.
所以我想我当时只是看着那个东西，然后随手涂鸦。

836
00:33:05.820 --> 00:33:11.420
And truth be told, there's only about three things I can draw in real life that look like the actual thing.
说实话，我现实中能画得像实物的也就三样东西。

837
00:33:11.560 --> 00:33:12.380
And one of them is a cat.
其中之一就是猫。

838
00:33:12.420 --> 00:33:13.220
One of them is a cat.
其中之一就是猫。

839
00:33:13.360 --> 00:33:14.460
That's kind of true for me too.
这点对我来说也差不多。

840
00:33:14.460 --> 00:33:15.560
I can draw a palm tree.
我会画棕榈树。

841
00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:16.760
I can draw a cat.
我会画猫。

842
00:33:17.620 --> 00:33:18.820
And I can draw Snoopy.
我还会画史努比。

843
00:33:19.460 --> 00:33:19.820
Hey!
嘿！

844
00:33:19.980 --> 00:33:20.600
There you go.
你看，这不就有了嘛。

845
00:33:20.780 --> 00:33:22.660
And I guess I had just doodled a cat.
我想我当时就是随手画了一只猫。

846
00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:24.320
And so I'd written on-
然后我就写在——

847
00:33:24.320 --> 00:33:29.260
So maybe my poor skills at drawing is also what gave birth to this moment.
所以也许是我拙劣的画技促成了这一刻。

848
00:33:29.260 --> 00:33:30.700
But I drew this cat and I wrote,
但我画了这只猫，写道：

849
00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:32.760
You're invited to Sprinkle's birthday party in the parking lot.
你被邀请参加斯普林克尔在停车场举办的生日派对。

850
00:33:32.840 --> 00:33:33.740
And you gave it to me.
然后你把它给了我。

851
00:33:33.820 --> 00:33:35.200
I handed it to you earlier.
我之前递给你了。

852
00:33:35.200 --> 00:33:35.600
I remember.
我记得。

853
00:33:35.760 --> 00:33:37.000
And it was weird.
而且那感觉很奇怪。

854
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:39.940
I remember getting it in the background of the scene and thinking,
我记得在拍摄背景里拿到它时，我心想，

855
00:33:39.960 --> 00:33:41.520
I don't know what this is.
我不知道这是什么。

856
00:33:41.760 --> 00:33:43.640
But I stuck it to my computer monitor.
但我把它贴在了我的电脑显示器上。

857
00:33:43.780 --> 00:33:44.780
Yeah, it was on a Post-it.
没错，它贴在一张便利贴上。

858
00:33:44.840 --> 00:33:46.060
And you stuck it to your computer.
而你把它贴在了你的电脑上。

859
00:33:46.720 --> 00:33:50.580
So when Ken Coapis asked me to talk to John about anything,
所以当肯·科阿皮斯让我和约翰聊点什么，

860
00:33:50.840 --> 00:33:53.160
to do this scene, just talk to each other,
为了拍这场戏，随便聊聊的时候，

861
00:33:53.340 --> 00:33:55.180
I noticed that Post-it note.
我注意到了那张便利贴。

862
00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:56.480
And I said,
于是我说，

863
00:33:56.820 --> 00:33:57.460
Are you going to go?
你会去吗？

864
00:33:57.620 --> 00:33:58.220
Something like-
大概是这样——

865
00:33:58.220 --> 00:34:00.280
To Angela's cat party on Sunday.
去安吉拉周日的猫咪派对。

866
00:34:00.580 --> 00:34:01.180
And he-
然后他——

867
00:34:01.180 --> 00:34:02.380
He's like, oh no, it's ridiculous.
他说，噢不，那太荒唐了。

868
00:34:02.560 --> 00:34:03.620
He's like, no, definitely not.
他说，不，绝对不去。

869
00:34:03.640 --> 00:34:04.580
And then we giggle.
然后我们就咯咯笑了起来。

870
00:34:04.940 --> 00:34:07.880
And that is the bit that they left in the episode.
而那段被保留在了剧集里。

871
00:34:08.100 --> 00:34:09.580
And that's the birth of Sprinkles.
那就是“斯普林克尔斯”的诞生。

872
00:34:09.720 --> 00:34:11.720
That was the birth of Sprinkles.
那是“斯普林克尔斯”的诞生。

873
00:34:11.820 --> 00:34:12.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

874
00:34:12.320 --> 00:34:15.300
That turned into this cat birthday party.
那演变成了这场猫咪生日派对。

875
00:34:15.420 --> 00:34:16.520
Greg honed in on that.
格雷格注意到了这一点。

876
00:34:16.620 --> 00:34:18.160
He was like, what is the cat birthday party?
他问，猫咪生日派对是什么？

877
00:34:18.300 --> 00:34:20.700
And I said, well, Angela gave me this Post-it note
我说，嗯，安吉拉给了我这张便利贴，

878
00:34:21.260 --> 00:34:24.120
about her birthday party for her cat or something.
关于她给猫办的生日派对之类的。

879
00:34:24.380 --> 00:34:24.540
Yeah.
没错。

880
00:34:24.640 --> 00:34:25.480
And he loved it.
他很喜欢这个点子。

881
00:34:25.560 --> 00:34:28.040
And then for four seasons-
然后接下来的四季——

882
00:34:28.040 --> 00:34:28.300
Yes.
是的。

883
00:34:28.440 --> 00:34:30.280
We discussed Sprinkles-
我们都在讨论斯普林克尔斯——

884
00:34:30.280 --> 00:34:31.880
Until his untimely death in the freezer.
直到它在冷冻柜里不幸离世。

885
00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:33.600
Yes, but that's another episode.
是的，但那是另一集的事了。

886
00:34:33.600 --> 00:34:35.200
I won't make you think about it.
我不会让你去想那件事的。

887
00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:36.780
Because it's one of my favorite Michael moments, too.
因为那也是我最喜欢的迈克尔时刻之一。

888
00:34:37.340 --> 00:34:39.400
Yeah, so that was really fun,
是啊，那真的很有趣，

889
00:34:39.520 --> 00:34:41.740
how just these little elements of us in the background
我们这些在背景里的小动作，

890
00:34:41.740 --> 00:34:45.280
sort of being bored and improvising made it into the show.
那种无聊时的即兴发挥，竟然被放进了剧里。

891
00:34:45.440 --> 00:34:45.660
Yeah.
没错。

892
00:34:45.660 --> 00:34:46.700
It's so special to me.
这对我来说太特别了。

893
00:34:47.000 --> 00:34:51.220
All right, so I have something that I am so curious about.
好了，我有一件特别好奇的事。

894
00:34:51.380 --> 00:34:52.760
And Jenna, I don't even know if you know this.
珍娜，我甚至不知道你知不知道这件事。

895
00:34:52.940 --> 00:34:54.820
Fans out there, I don't know if you know it
各位粉丝，我不知道你们知不知道，

896
00:34:54.820 --> 00:34:58.600
or if we need to text Dave Rogers, our editor extraordinaire.
或者我们是否需要给我们的超级剪辑师戴夫·罗杰斯发条短信。

897
00:34:58.780 --> 00:35:02.520
So my D'Angela fans, did you notice in the pilot episode
所以，我的“迪安吉拉”粉丝们，你们有没有注意到在试播集中，

898
00:35:02.520 --> 00:35:05.380
that Dwight is singing Little Drummer Boy
德怀特在整理办公桌时，

899
00:35:05.380 --> 00:35:07.500
as he unpacks his desk?
在唱《小鼓手男孩》？

900
00:35:08.280 --> 00:35:08.720
Angela.
安吉拉。

901
00:35:09.040 --> 00:35:11.660
He's singing like, come, they told me.
他唱的是，来吧，他们告诉我。

902
00:35:12.100 --> 00:35:12.540
Yes.
是的。

903
00:35:12.540 --> 00:35:14.660
But then he goes, do-do-do-do, do-do-do-do-do.
然后他唱，嘟嘟嘟嘟，嘟嘟嘟嘟嘟。

904
00:35:14.660 --> 00:35:21.160
And then in season three, I karaoke Little Drummer Boy
后来在第三季，我唱了《小鼓手男孩》的卡拉OK，

905
00:35:21.160 --> 00:35:23.340
and Dwight joins in and sings with me.
德怀特也加入进来和我一起唱。

906
00:35:23.720 --> 00:35:27.240
Now, that story is that I was very nervous to sing.
那个故事是说，我当时唱歌非常紧张。

907
00:35:27.400 --> 00:35:28.780
I don't like singing in front of people.
我不喜欢在别人面前唱歌。

908
00:35:29.040 --> 00:35:32.600
And Rain, as Dwight, just jumped in and kind of like supported me
而雷恩，作为德怀特，直接加入进来，算是支持了我，

909
00:35:32.600 --> 00:35:33.740
so I wasn't up there alone.
这样我就不是一个人站在那儿了。

910
00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:36.460
And he kneeled down and he held the microphone for me.
他跪下来，还帮我拿着麦克风。

911
00:35:36.760 --> 00:35:38.580
And I'm just like, oh my God.
我当时心想，天哪。

912
00:35:39.120 --> 00:35:40.980
I mean, what?
我是说，什么情况？

913
00:35:41.220 --> 00:35:41.960
That's weird.
这太奇怪了。

914
00:35:42.440 --> 00:35:44.860
I feel like that has to be a coincidence.
我觉得这一定是个巧合。

915
00:35:45.260 --> 00:35:46.420
I think it's a coincidence.
我认为这就是个巧合。

916
00:35:46.640 --> 00:35:52.420
But how, and so many fans say to me, like, what amazing synergy it is
但怎么会呢，很多粉丝都跟我说，这配合简直太绝了，

917
00:35:52.420 --> 00:35:55.200
that Dwight is singing Little Drummer Boy in the pilot.
德怀特在试播集中唱了《小鼓手男孩》。

918
00:35:55.460 --> 00:35:58.360
And then in season three, I sing it to him.
然后在第三季，我唱给他听。

919
00:35:58.720 --> 00:36:00.220
Now, did a writer remember that?
那么，是有编剧记得这件事吗？

920
00:36:00.340 --> 00:36:04.440
Was that something that like, or was that just in the subconscious of the show?
那是刻意为之，还是仅仅存在于剧集的潜意识里？

921
00:36:04.540 --> 00:36:05.080
I don't know.
我不知道。

922
00:36:05.180 --> 00:36:05.540
I don't know.
我不知道。

923
00:36:05.620 --> 00:36:06.620
You know what I found?
你知道我发现了什么吗？

924
00:36:06.620 --> 00:36:10.300
I found this article, and I can't remember where.
我找到了这篇文章，但不记得是在哪儿看到的了。

925
00:36:10.400 --> 00:36:10.900
I apologize.
抱歉。

926
00:36:11.280 --> 00:36:16.340
I found an article that was all about secret messages in the pilot episode.
我找到了一篇关于试播集中隐藏信息的文章。

927
00:36:16.860 --> 00:36:22.260
And one of the secret messages that someone points out is that in the scene where Roy
其中有人指出的一个隐藏信息是，在罗伊

928
00:36:22.260 --> 00:36:26.600
comes in the door for the first time, the boom mic dips into frame.
第一次进门的那场戏里，吊杆麦克风穿帮入镜了。

929
00:36:27.860 --> 00:36:34.420
And someone wondered, was that a nod to the boom operator, Brian, that we will meet in
有人好奇，这是否是在向我们在第九季中

930
00:36:34.420 --> 00:36:35.200
season nine?
才会见到的收音师布莱恩致意？

931
00:36:35.420 --> 00:36:37.040
No, that was just an accident.
不，那只是个意外。

932
00:36:37.580 --> 00:36:46.680
Was it foreshadowing to let us know that there are three men in Pam's life, Jim, Roy, and Brian?
那是为了预示帕姆生命中有三个男人：吉姆、罗伊和布莱恩吗？

933
00:36:47.120 --> 00:36:47.540
No, no.
不，不是。

934
00:36:47.600 --> 00:36:50.900
That was just a boom operator accident, and they left it in because it's a documentary.
那只是收音师的失误，因为是纪录片风格，所以他们就保留了。

935
00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:53.100
Yes, we left that stuff in all the time.
是的，我们一直都会保留这类素材。

936
00:36:53.100 --> 00:36:56.340
That was a thing that we coveted that.
那是我们梦寐以求的东西。

937
00:36:56.540 --> 00:36:57.220
We loved it.
我们很喜欢那样。

938
00:36:57.320 --> 00:37:03.260
If the camera person fumbled or if the boom accidentally wasn't shot, we still used it,
如果摄影师失误了，或者吊杆麦克风意外穿帮了，我们照样会用，

939
00:37:03.280 --> 00:37:03.920
and we could.
而且我们确实能用。

940
00:37:04.080 --> 00:37:09.680
And that was actually great because sometimes you're on a set, and your best take is ruined
这其实很棒，因为有时候你在片场，最好的表演却因为

941
00:37:09.680 --> 00:37:14.100
because of some technical accident on the set.
片场的一些技术失误而被毁了。

942
00:37:14.240 --> 00:37:15.940
But we were able to use all of it.
但我们能够把这些全部用上。

943
00:37:16.020 --> 00:37:17.800
We didn't have to put it on the cutting room floor.
我们不必把它们剪掉扔进垃圾桶。

944
00:37:18.040 --> 00:37:19.340
Okay, so yeah, so no conspiracy.
好吧，所以说，并没有什么阴谋论。

945
00:37:19.340 --> 00:37:23.760
But yeah, I don't know if Dwight singing Little Drummer Boy in the pilot and Angela singing
不过，我不知道德怀特在试播集中唱《小鼓手男孩》，和安吉拉在

946
00:37:23.760 --> 00:37:29.700
it in Benihana Christmas in season three is just a crazy coincidence, but it's cool, right?
第三季的《圣诞派对》中唱这首歌，是否只是一个疯狂的巧合，但这很酷，对吧？

947
00:37:29.820 --> 00:37:30.900
It's a pretty cool observation.
这是一个非常酷的观察。

948
00:37:30.900 --> 00:37:31.080
It's pretty cool.
真的很酷。

949
00:37:31.380 --> 00:37:36.760
I actually really love these fan theories because I like to think that these accidents
我其实非常喜欢这些粉丝理论，因为我愿意认为这些意外

950
00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:42.080
or coincidences, if they are accidents, are part of a fun, collective, unconscious
或者巧合——如果它们确实是意外的话——是某种有趣的集体潜意识的一部分。

951
00:37:42.080 --> 00:37:44.960
thing that kind of lend itself to the magic of the show.
这某种程度上造就了这部剧的魔力。

952
00:37:45.740 --> 00:37:48.240
Wow, Jenna, that was really deep.
哇，珍娜，这真的很深刻。

953
00:37:48.240 --> 00:37:49.140
I kind of was.
我刚才确实有点。

954
00:37:49.220 --> 00:37:50.780
I got real philosophical there.
我刚才变得很哲学。

955
00:37:50.940 --> 00:37:55.040
Oh my gosh, I feel like I just had like a vision of what you were like in college or
天哪，我感觉我刚才仿佛看到了你大学时的样子，

956
00:37:55.040 --> 00:37:55.360
something.
或者类似的情景。

957
00:37:55.560 --> 00:37:55.740
Yeah.
是啊。

958
00:37:55.900 --> 00:38:00.760
Like you sat around, like maybe like you wore like black turtlenecks and like, I don't
就像你坐在那儿，可能穿着黑色高领毛衣，

959
00:38:00.760 --> 00:38:00.810
know.
我不知道。

960
00:38:00.920 --> 00:38:03.580
I was kind of like, I was kind of like Art Show Pam.
我当时有点像，有点像“艺术展帕姆”。

961
00:38:03.940 --> 00:38:04.640
Art Show Pam!
“艺术展帕姆”！

962
00:38:04.640 --> 00:38:05.420
With my turtleneck.
穿着我的高领毛衣。

963
00:38:05.600 --> 00:38:05.720
Yeah.
没错。

964
00:38:05.720 --> 00:38:06.360
My jumper.
还有我的毛线背心。

965
00:38:06.600 --> 00:38:07.420
Well, I like it.
嗯，我喜欢这个形象。

966
00:38:07.440 --> 00:38:08.200
Spilling philosophy.
满口哲学。

967
00:38:08.560 --> 00:38:10.140
All right, Angela, what have you got for us?
好了，安吉拉，你有什么要分享的吗？

968
00:38:10.260 --> 00:38:13.740
I only had one speaking scene in the pilot and so did Brian.
在试播集中，我和布莱恩都只有一句台词。

969
00:38:13.740 --> 00:38:18.240
It was back in accounting when Angela and Kevin are trying to figure out who's going to be
那是在会计部，安吉拉和凯文正试图弄清楚谁会因为裁员

970
00:38:18.240 --> 00:38:19.380
fired for downsizing.
而被解雇。

971
00:38:19.600 --> 00:38:21.740
We were really nervous about shooting the scene.
我们当时拍那场戏时真的很紧张。

972
00:38:21.860 --> 00:38:23.160
It's the only time we speak.
那是我们唯一开口说话的时候。

973
00:38:23.460 --> 00:38:28.700
And it was at the end of the day, Ken Quapas, who's, you know, we've said the nicest guy,
那天快结束时，肯·夸帕斯，你知道的，我们说过他是最好的人，

974
00:38:28.820 --> 00:38:29.760
was like, go ahead.
他说，开始吧。

975
00:38:30.360 --> 00:38:32.860
And I said, somebody's going to be fired.
我说，有人要被解雇了。

976
00:38:32.900 --> 00:38:34.000
It'll probably be me.
那个人可能会是我。

977
00:38:34.180 --> 00:38:36.520
And Brian, as Kevin says, yeah, it'll probably be you.
然后布莱恩，也就是凯文，说，是啊，那个人可能会是你。

978
00:38:37.960 --> 00:38:41.160
And Ken came up to me and goes, hey, Angela, can you do it again?
肯走过来对我说，嘿，安吉拉，你能再来一次吗？

979
00:38:41.280 --> 00:38:43.340
And like, just give it like half.
就，力度减半。

980
00:38:43.760 --> 00:38:44.640
Give it half.
减半。

981
00:38:45.620 --> 00:38:47.320
So I guess I was like, was I too big?
所以我当时想，是我演得太夸张了吗？

982
00:38:47.440 --> 00:38:48.600
Was I like, somebody's going to be fired.
我是不是演成了“有人要被解雇了！”

983
00:38:48.660 --> 00:38:49.380
It'll probably be me.
“那个人可能会是我！”

984
00:38:49.920 --> 00:38:52.520
And then so I was like, somebody will probably be fired.
于是我试着说，有人可能会被解雇。

985
00:38:52.580 --> 00:38:53.220
It'll probably be me.
那个人可能会是我。

986
00:38:53.860 --> 00:38:54.540
Someone's going to get fired.
有人要被解雇了。

987
00:38:54.680 --> 00:38:55.760
Is that the exact line?
那是原台词吗？

988
00:38:55.920 --> 00:38:56.740
Somebody's going to be fired.
有人要被解雇了。

989
00:38:56.880 --> 00:38:57.540
It'll probably be me.
那个人可能会是我。

990
00:38:57.980 --> 00:39:00.220
Then he came up and he goes, half of that.
然后他走过来又说，再减半。

991
00:39:01.080 --> 00:39:01.900
I said, oh, OK.
我说，哦，好的。

992
00:39:02.560 --> 00:39:04.120
So then I was like, somebody's going to be fired.
于是我试着说，有人要被解雇了。

993
00:39:04.160 --> 00:39:04.840
It'll probably be me.
那个人可能会是我。

994
00:39:05.560 --> 00:39:08.060
And he goes, half of that.
他又说，再减半。

995
00:39:08.240 --> 00:39:13.500
And I said, oh, my God, I'm going to get fired because I'm like an improv sketch comedy actor
我说，天哪，我要被解雇了，因为我像个即兴喜剧演员，

996
00:39:13.500 --> 00:39:14.760
and clearly I'm too broad.
显然我演得太浮夸了。

997
00:39:14.960 --> 00:39:19.100
And so ultimately, the take they use, by the end of it, I literally was like,
最终，他们采用的那一版，到最后，我真的变成了这样：

998
00:39:20.340 --> 00:39:21.600
somebody's going to be fired.
有人要被解雇了。

999
00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:22.400
It'll probably be me.
那个人可能会是我。

1000
00:39:23.020 --> 00:39:24.680
And then Brian's like, yeah, it'll probably be you.
然后布莱恩说，是啊，那个人可能会是你。

1001
00:39:24.880 --> 00:39:26.300
And Ken was like, we got it.
然后肯就说，我们搞定了。

1002
00:39:26.460 --> 00:39:27.040
I was like.
我就说。

1003
00:39:27.280 --> 00:39:30.960
Do you want to point out what you noticed about this scene as well about Kevin?
你也要指出你在这场戏里注意到的关于凯文的事情吗？

1004
00:39:31.340 --> 00:39:34.360
Here's my tidbit, guys, is that when I watched this,
伙计们，这是我的发现，当我看到这一幕时，

1005
00:39:34.360 --> 00:39:38.360
and Brian, I want to call you about it, you just sound like Brian to me.
布莱恩，我想就这件事给你打电话，你听起来就像布莱恩。

1006
00:39:38.480 --> 00:39:40.020
You don't sound like the Kevin voice.
你听起来不像凯文的声音。

1007
00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:41.020
OK, can we play it?
好吧，我们可以播放它吗？

1008
00:39:41.280 --> 00:39:42.700
I bet it's going to be me.
我敢打赌那会是我。

1009
00:39:42.940 --> 00:39:43.340
Probably.
大概吧。

1010
00:39:43.600 --> 00:39:44.100
It's going to be me.
那会是我。

1011
00:39:45.260 --> 00:39:46.340
Yeah, it'll be you.
没错，会是你。

1012
00:39:46.840 --> 00:39:47.420
That's Brian!
那是布莱恩！

1013
00:39:47.420 --> 00:39:48.520
Oh, my gosh!
天哪！

1014
00:39:48.660 --> 00:39:49.340
That's Brian!
那是布莱恩！

1015
00:39:49.740 --> 00:39:50.980
That is Brian's voice.
那是布莱恩的声音。

1016
00:39:51.140 --> 00:39:51.520
That's not.
那不是。

1017
00:39:51.600 --> 00:39:54.460
Because Kevin would have been like, yeah, it'll probably be me.
因为凯文会说，嗯，大概会是我。

1018
00:39:54.460 --> 00:39:55.680
It'll probably be me.
大概会是我。

1019
00:39:55.800 --> 00:39:55.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1020
00:39:56.020 --> 00:39:56.860
That's a horrible Kevin.
那是个糟糕的凯文模仿。

1021
00:39:56.900 --> 00:39:58.860
We just really did not do that well.
我们真的没演好。

1022
00:39:58.860 --> 00:39:59.280
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1023
00:39:59.280 --> 00:40:00.660
I want to call Brian about it.
我想就这件事给布莱恩打电话。

1024
00:40:00.780 --> 00:40:03.000
But when I watched it, I was like, wait a second.
但当我观看时，我就想，等一下。

1025
00:40:03.540 --> 00:40:04.700
It's like, that's Brian.
就像是，那是布莱恩。

1026
00:40:05.220 --> 00:40:10.120
But I think in the pilot, we were still sort of like figuring out our characters and who they were.
但我觉得在试播集中，我们还在摸索各自的角色以及他们是谁。

1027
00:40:10.760 --> 00:40:12.800
However, I have to say, Angela.
不过，安吉拉，我得说。

1028
00:40:13.060 --> 00:40:13.240
What?
什么？

1029
00:40:13.420 --> 00:40:15.680
I went into the deleted scenes.
我看了删减片段。

1030
00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:16.560
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1031
00:40:16.560 --> 00:40:18.720
On the DVD, season one DVD.
在DVD上，第一季的DVD。

1032
00:40:19.160 --> 00:40:19.440
And?
然后呢？

1033
00:40:19.540 --> 00:40:23.400
And there is, this is something we did on the pilot.
然后有，这是我们在试播集里做过的事情。

1034
00:40:23.720 --> 00:40:29.620
Some of it was an acting exercise where they called us each into the conference room separately.
其中一些是表演练习，他们把我们每个人分别叫进会议室。

1035
00:40:29.620 --> 00:40:36.380
And they just asked us unscripted lines about our characters and about our relationship to other characters.
他们只是问了我们一些关于角色以及我们与其他角色关系的即兴台词。

1036
00:40:36.540 --> 00:40:37.420
I remember this.
我记得这个。

1037
00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:38.040
It wasn't written.
那不是写好的。

1038
00:40:38.060 --> 00:40:38.760
It was not written.
那不是写好的。

1039
00:40:38.800 --> 00:40:39.860
We just improvised.
我们只是即兴发挥。

1040
00:40:39.860 --> 00:40:46.320
Oh, so this was sort of, I think, an exercise that Ken wanted to do that Greg and Ken came up with.
哦，所以我想这大概是肯想做的一个练习，是格雷格和肯想出来的。

1041
00:40:46.460 --> 00:40:52.920
In addition to that thing where they filmed us all just working, they also filmed us being interviewed in character.
除了拍摄我们所有人工作的片段外，他们还拍摄了我们以角色身份接受采访的画面。

1042
00:40:53.200 --> 00:40:54.720
And I think Greg thought, this will be great.
我想格雷格觉得，这会很棒。

1043
00:40:54.780 --> 00:40:57.400
Maybe I could use some of these little tidbits here and there.
也许我可以在这里或那里用上这些小花絮。

1044
00:40:57.720 --> 00:41:01.700
Well, there is a series of interviews with each of the members of accounting.
嗯，有一系列对会计部每位成员的采访。

1045
00:41:01.940 --> 00:41:02.540
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1046
00:41:02.580 --> 00:41:06.580
Where you guys are all trash talking each other very subtly.
你们所有人都在非常含蓄地互相说坏话。

1047
00:41:07.360 --> 00:41:14.880
And Angela, you have this incredible deleted scene talking head where they ask you about Oscar.
安吉拉，你有一个令人难以置信的删减采访片段，他们问你关于奥斯卡的事。

1048
00:41:15.180 --> 00:41:17.000
Is this where I compare him to a stapler?
就是我把他比作订书机的那段吗？

1049
00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:17.840
Yes.
是的。

1050
00:41:18.120 --> 00:41:20.100
Sam, can you pull that up so we can listen to that?
萨姆，你能把它调出来让我们听听吗？

1051
00:41:20.260 --> 00:41:21.620
Oscar, how do I describe him?
奥斯卡，我该怎么形容他呢？

1052
00:41:22.140 --> 00:41:23.800
He's like a stapler.
他就像个订书机。

1053
00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:25.620
Do I need a stapler?
我需要订书机吗？

1054
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:26.160
Yes.
需要。

1055
00:41:26.900 --> 00:41:29.440
But I'm still the one that has to push it down.
但还得是我亲手把它按下去才行。

1056
00:41:29.640 --> 00:41:30.180
I did.
我当时是这么说的。

1057
00:41:30.180 --> 00:41:34.980
I improvised that because I was trying to think of, like, what, like, how does Angela see Oscar?
那是我的即兴发挥，因为我在想，安吉拉是怎么看待奥斯卡的？

1058
00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:39.680
And he's just, like, he's necessary, but he's a, he ends up being more work for her.
他就是那种，虽然必不可少，但最终却只会给她增加工作量的人。

1059
00:41:39.820 --> 00:41:40.160
Yes.
没错。

1060
00:41:40.160 --> 00:41:40.920
But he's annoying.
但他很烦人。

1061
00:41:41.260 --> 00:41:48.260
What was so clear to me when I was watching them was this accounting dynamic had already started.
我在看他们的时候，非常清楚地感觉到这种会计部的动态关系已经开始了。

1062
00:41:48.560 --> 00:41:48.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1063
00:41:48.740 --> 00:41:55.240
This little pod that you guys form, this little trio, it was there from the very beginning.
你们形成的这个小团体，这个三人组，从一开始就在那儿了。

1064
00:41:55.780 --> 00:42:00.460
Also, I do have to point, fans, all of the deleted scenes are fantastic.
另外，我必须得提醒粉丝们，所有的删减片段都很精彩。

1065
00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:03.320
Rainn Wilson has some talking heads.
雷恩·威尔森有一些采访片段。

1066
00:42:03.320 --> 00:42:11.160
There is a long, extended, deleted scene-talking head of him talking to Ken Quapis, who played the documentarian for us.
有一个很长的、扩展的删减采访片段，是他和肯·夸皮斯对话，肯在剧中扮演我们的纪录片导演。

1067
00:42:11.200 --> 00:42:16.260
He would ask us the questions, our director, all about where the boom microphone was.
他会问我们问题，我们的导演，全是关于吊杆麦克风在哪里的问题。

1068
00:42:17.100 --> 00:42:20.680
Rainn, as Dwight, was very distracted by the boom.
雷恩饰演的德怀特，被那个麦克风弄得很分心。

1069
00:42:21.020 --> 00:42:21.680
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1070
00:42:21.700 --> 00:42:24.200
And he was saying, I really need you to move that.
他说，我真的需要你把它移开。

1071
00:42:24.480 --> 00:42:26.300
Ken says, we can put it in your blind spot.
肯说，我们可以把它放在你的盲区。

1072
00:42:26.300 --> 00:42:28.280
And he says something like, I don't have a blind spot.
然后他说，我没有盲区。

1073
00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:31.200
I've been trained, so it's especially distracting for me.
我受过训练，所以这对我来说特别容易分心。

1074
00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:33.120
You need to understand that I'm highly trained.
你需要明白，我可是受过高等训练的。

1075
00:42:33.260 --> 00:42:40.480
And it's just this little, like, non-presentational conversation between Dwight and the documentarian about how to be mic'd.
这只是德怀特和纪录片导演之间一段非常随意的、非正式的关于如何收音的对话。

1076
00:42:40.520 --> 00:42:41.640
I just want to say one thing.
我只想说一件事。

1077
00:42:41.860 --> 00:42:46.300
So many great things that were established in the pilot that you go on to see for years to come.
试播集中确立了太多伟大的东西，你会在未来几年里一直看到它们。

1078
00:42:46.480 --> 00:42:49.500
Of course, one of the big ones is the Jim versus Dwight.
当然，其中最重要的一点就是吉姆和德怀特的对抗。

1079
00:42:49.500 --> 00:42:51.640
And, like, sort of their battle, right?
还有他们之间的那种较量，对吧？

1080
00:42:51.760 --> 00:42:54.280
And the pranks that Jim is going to do on Dwight.
以及吉姆要对德怀特搞的那些恶作剧。

1081
00:42:54.420 --> 00:43:00.460
And I love that it just started out so simply with Dwight pushing all of Jim's papers back to his desk.
我喜欢它最初只是那么简单，德怀特把吉姆所有的文件都推回了他的桌子上。

1082
00:43:00.480 --> 00:43:02.480
And then Jim making the pencil wall.
然后吉姆就筑起了一道铅笔墙。

1083
00:43:03.020 --> 00:43:04.200
It's just ridiculous.
这简直太荒谬了。

1084
00:43:04.740 --> 00:43:06.640
Well, that was borrowed from the British show.
嗯，那是借鉴了英版剧集。

1085
00:43:06.800 --> 00:43:08.940
In the British show, they have the same desk war.
在英版里，他们也有同样的办公桌战争。

1086
00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:12.320
But instead, the Jim character piles up a bunch of boxes.
但不同的是，吉姆那个角色堆了一堆盒子。

1087
00:43:12.480 --> 00:43:14.840
He makes a box wall between the desks.
他在两张桌子之间筑起了一道盒子墙。

1088
00:43:15.340 --> 00:43:17.620
And we did that when we filmed the pilot.
我们在拍摄试播集时也拍了那个版本。

1089
00:43:17.800 --> 00:43:19.980
We had Jim make a box wall.
我们让吉姆筑了一道盒子墙。

1090
00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:24.160
And, in fact, you can see it in the background of conference room scenes.
事实上，你可以在会议室场景的背景里看到它。

1091
00:43:24.300 --> 00:43:27.260
You can see a bunch of boxes piled up on Jim's desk.
你可以看到吉姆的桌子上堆了一堆盒子。

1092
00:43:27.340 --> 00:43:29.440
My lady, I'm going to go back and look.
女士，我回头一定要去看看。

1093
00:43:29.940 --> 00:43:36.460
Later, when we got picked up, we reshot that scene and turned it into a little pencil thing.
后来，当我们确定被续订后，我们重拍了那个场景，把它改成了铅笔墙。

1094
00:43:36.620 --> 00:43:42.580
And you can also see that Rain's hair is a little bit different in the pencil scene compared to the rest of the pilot.
你还可以发现，在铅笔墙的那个场景里，雷恩的头发和试播集其他部分相比有点不同。

1095
00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:43.380
It's not as poofy.
没那么蓬松。

1096
00:43:43.620 --> 00:43:44.220
That's right.
没错。

1097
00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:44.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1098
00:43:44.540 --> 00:43:45.120
Exactly.
确实。

1099
00:43:45.520 --> 00:43:51.620
Rain, as Dwight, went through poofy hair phase, which looks like they used a little miniature, like, rolling brush to blow dry his hair.
雷恩饰演的德怀特经历过蓬松发型阶段，看起来像是用了那种小型的圆筒梳来吹头发。

1100
00:43:51.780 --> 00:43:54.620
And then he went through flat, parted-down-the-middle phase.
然后他又经历过扁塌的中分发型阶段。

1101
00:43:54.800 --> 00:43:57.160
Well, Rain created the hairstyle for Dwight.
雷恩为德怀特设计了这个发型。

1102
00:43:57.220 --> 00:44:02.840
And he said before that it is based on the hairstyle that he wore when he was a 16-year-old boy.
他说过这个发型的灵感来自他16岁时留的发型。

1103
00:44:03.420 --> 00:44:05.460
And so he did his own hair for the pilot.
所以试播集里他的头发是他自己打理的。

1104
00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:06.960
That makes me laugh.
这让我觉得很好笑。

1105
00:44:07.140 --> 00:44:08.820
I've seen those photos of Rain.
我见过雷恩那些照片。

1106
00:44:09.080 --> 00:44:09.840
They're crazy.
太疯狂了。

1107
00:44:10.260 --> 00:44:11.720
You wore your own clothes in the pilot.
你在试播集里穿的是自己的衣服。

1108
00:44:11.760 --> 00:44:13.660
I wore my own clothes in the pilot.
我在试播集里穿的也是自己的衣服。

1109
00:44:13.660 --> 00:44:14.280
All right.
好吧。

1110
00:44:14.420 --> 00:44:22.580
So the last sort of thing I think we need to talk about is this big prank on Pam, quote-unquote, the scene where Michael fake fires her.
所以我觉得我们需要谈的最后一件事，就是那个针对帕姆的所谓“恶作剧”，也就是迈克尔假装解雇她的那场戏。

1111
00:44:22.580 --> 00:44:26.340
Well, he's so excited because Jim has had a very successful prank.
嗯，他当时很兴奋，因为吉姆刚搞了一个非常成功的恶作剧。

1112
00:44:26.560 --> 00:44:29.000
And Michael just, he wants to be in the spotlight.
而迈克尔只是想成为焦点。

1113
00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:30.260
He wants to be the funny guy.
他想当那个搞笑的人。

1114
00:44:30.260 --> 00:44:34.680
So he's going to show off for Ryan the 10th, and he's going to fake fire Pam.
所以他要在瑞安面前炫耀一下，于是他决定假装解雇帕姆。

1115
00:44:35.060 --> 00:44:38.000
And it, of course, goes horribly wrong, and she ends up in tears.
当然，结果搞砸了，她最后哭了起来。

1116
00:44:38.180 --> 00:44:42.380
And we shot that scene probably 30 times.
那场戏我们大概拍了30遍。

1117
00:44:42.580 --> 00:44:42.840
Wow.
哇。

1118
00:44:42.840 --> 00:44:48.320
And at the beginning of the scene, you can see everyone in the background kind of getting ready to leave for the day.
在戏刚开始的时候，你可以看到背景里每个人都准备下班了。

1119
00:44:49.440 --> 00:44:52.740
And all those people had to wait for hours.
那些人都等了几个小时。

1120
00:44:53.080 --> 00:44:56.580
They would have to start in the background, and then we would do this whole scene.
他们得先在背景里就位，然后我们再演整场戏。

1121
00:44:56.620 --> 00:44:57.920
Oh, I know, Jenna.
哦，我知道，珍娜。

1122
00:44:58.040 --> 00:44:58.500
I know.
我知道。

1123
00:44:58.800 --> 00:44:59.760
I was there.
我也在场。

1124
00:44:59.940 --> 00:45:03.020
I had to grab my jacket, my coat, and my purse, put them down.
我得抓起我的夹克、外套和包，然后放下。

1125
00:45:03.120 --> 00:45:04.000
My coat and my purse.
我的外套和我的包。

1126
00:45:04.000 --> 00:45:11.340
I think of any scene in the entire history of The Office, this is the one that I've done the most because we did about 30 takes of it that day.
我觉得在《办公室》整部剧的历史中，这是我拍过次数最多的一场戏，因为那天我们拍了大约30条。

1127
00:45:11.420 --> 00:45:13.320
But it was also my audition scene.
但这也是我的试镜戏份。

1128
00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:15.620
This was one of my audition scenes.
这是我试镜时的戏份之一。

1129
00:45:15.760 --> 00:45:19.440
And so I auditioned for months for this role.
我为了这个角色试镜了好几个月。

1130
00:45:19.680 --> 00:45:24.220
I did that scene one time when I auditioned for the role of Pam, and I didn't get it.
我试镜帕姆这个角色时演过一次那场戏，但我没选上。

1131
00:45:25.460 --> 00:45:28.580
This is such a crazy, crazy bit of trivia.
这真是一个超级疯狂的冷知识。

1132
00:45:28.600 --> 00:45:29.200
Yes, yes.
没错，没错。

1133
00:45:29.320 --> 00:45:32.080
Your first audition for The Office was for the role of Pam.
你第一次参加《办公室》试镜时，试的是帕姆这个角色。

1134
00:45:32.080 --> 00:45:35.440
It was for the role of Pam, and I wore a pink sweater.
确实是帕姆这个角色，我当时穿了一件粉色毛衣。

1135
00:45:35.760 --> 00:45:36.080
What?
什么？

1136
00:45:36.240 --> 00:45:36.380
Yes.
是的。

1137
00:45:36.380 --> 00:45:37.440
We both had the same instinct.
我们俩的直觉一样。

1138
00:45:37.620 --> 00:45:38.700
Pam wears pink sweater.
帕姆就穿粉色毛衣。

1139
00:45:38.880 --> 00:45:45.400
I wore a pink sweater and my hair down, and I was told to look, you know, like not too fancy, so I didn't do too much with my hair and makeup.
我穿了一件粉色毛衣，披散着头发，有人告诉我看起来不要太精致，所以我没怎么打理头发和妆容。

1140
00:45:45.620 --> 00:45:50.280
And I went in, and I did the scene, and it was for a room full of people, the producers.
我走进去演了那场戏，当时房间里坐满了制片人。

1141
00:45:50.760 --> 00:45:56.200
And when we got to the point where Michael fake fires you, and you start to cry, and you call him a jerk.
当我们演到迈克尔假装解雇你，你开始哭，并骂他是混蛋的时候。

1142
00:45:56.420 --> 00:45:56.640
Yeah.
没错。

1143
00:45:57.100 --> 00:46:00.040
When I called him a jerk, everyone started to laugh.
当我骂他是混蛋时，所有人都笑了起来。

1144
00:46:00.160 --> 00:46:01.880
And I thought, I did something wrong.
我当时心想，我肯定做错什么了。

1145
00:46:02.360 --> 00:46:04.300
I don't think they're supposed to laugh at this moment.
我觉得在这个时刻他们不该笑的。

1146
00:46:04.520 --> 00:46:12.600
And of course, like, Jenna, you were so brilliant because you brought such a vulnerability to Pam that even though this job sucks and she hates it, she needs it.
当然了，珍娜，你当时表现得太出色了，因为你为帕姆注入了一种脆弱感，即使这份工作很烂，她很讨厌它，但她确实需要它。

1147
00:46:12.740 --> 00:46:14.400
She needs this crappy job.
她需要这份糟糕的工作。

1148
00:46:14.500 --> 00:46:14.660
Yeah.
没错。

1149
00:46:14.660 --> 00:46:17.420
And you really felt her in that moment.
那一刻你真的让人感同身受。

1150
00:46:17.600 --> 00:46:19.360
You just, my heart broke for her.
你真的……我当时心都碎了。

1151
00:46:19.780 --> 00:46:23.600
And when you call him a jerk, it's just like you're really wounded.
当你骂他混蛋的时候，看起来就像是你真的受伤了。

1152
00:46:23.640 --> 00:46:28.120
And it checks Michael in his place of like, that wasn't cool.
这让迈克尔意识到自己的位置，意识到那样做并不妥。

1153
00:46:28.280 --> 00:46:28.720
Right?
对吧？

1154
00:46:28.720 --> 00:46:33.320
It's funny because this was a somewhat controversial scene about whether or not it should be included.
有趣的是，关于这一幕是否应该保留，当时还有些争议。

1155
00:46:33.520 --> 00:46:41.620
When Ricky and Steven were counseling Greg, I understand that they told him that he should consider cutting the scene.
当瑞奇和史蒂文在给格雷格提建议时，我听说他们告诉他应该考虑删掉这一幕。

1156
00:46:41.620 --> 00:46:48.820
Because they said that it's in their pilot and they felt like they always had to fight to come back from it.
因为他们说这出现在试播集中，他们觉得如果不删掉，以后很难挽回观众对角色的好感。

1157
00:46:48.980 --> 00:46:52.020
That it made the boss a little too mean.
因为这让老板显得太刻薄了。

1158
00:46:52.020 --> 00:46:57.480
And so later they really leaned into his buffoonery.
所以后来他们真的更侧重于表现他的愚蠢。

1159
00:46:58.180 --> 00:47:00.000
But Greg fought to keep it in.
但格雷格坚持要保留这一幕。

1160
00:47:00.120 --> 00:47:02.840
He thought, no, we're going to try it.
他想，不，我们要试一试。

1161
00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:04.040
We're going to let her cry.
我们要让她哭出来。

1162
00:47:04.200 --> 00:47:05.960
We're going to let Michael be mean to her.
我们要让迈克尔对她刻薄一点。

1163
00:47:05.960 --> 00:47:13.680
Now, there was an alt line where I think that sometimes instead of saying you're a jerk, I said you're a sad little man.
当时还有一句备选台词，我想有时候我不说“你是个混蛋”，而是说“你是个可悲的小男人”。

1164
00:47:14.640 --> 00:47:16.840
And they said that's too harsh.
他们说那太伤人了。

1165
00:47:17.700 --> 00:47:19.300
You can't come back from that.
那样的话就没法挽回了。

1166
00:47:19.600 --> 00:47:20.560
That is harsh.
那确实很伤人。

1167
00:47:20.780 --> 00:47:24.020
So here's a little fun tidbit, Jenna.
所以这里有个有趣的小花絮，珍娜。

1168
00:47:24.180 --> 00:47:26.100
Another tidbit, not a fast fact.
又是一个花絮，不是冷知识。

1169
00:47:26.180 --> 00:47:27.380
A tidbit from Angela Kinsey.
来自安吉拉·金赛的花絮。

1170
00:47:27.380 --> 00:47:36.400
When Michael wants to prank Pam in front of Ryan the Temp, Michael, as Steve, turns to Ryan, BJ, and says, have you ever seen, you know, do you like prank shows?
当迈克尔想在临时工瑞安面前捉弄帕姆时，迈克尔，也就是史蒂夫，转向瑞安，也就是BJ，说，你有没有看过，你知道，你喜欢恶搞节目吗？

1171
00:47:36.620 --> 00:47:37.600
Have you ever seen Punk'd?
你看过《整蛊总动员》吗？

1172
00:47:38.500 --> 00:47:39.740
BJ was on Punk'd.
BJ上过《整蛊总动员》。

1173
00:47:39.740 --> 00:47:40.460
He was on Punk'd.
他上过那个节目。

1174
00:47:40.460 --> 00:47:41.840
He was on season two of Punk'd.
他参加了《整蛊总动员》第二季。

1175
00:47:41.880 --> 00:47:47.720
So I thought that was a nice little nod that he's looking at someone who was on Punk'd and says, do you like Punk'd?
所以我认为这是一个很好的致敬，他看着一个上过《整蛊总动员》的人，问他喜不喜欢《整蛊总动员》？

1176
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:49.980
And BJ's like, yeah, like as Ryan.
而BJ回答说，喜欢，是以瑞安的身份回答的。

1177
00:47:50.440 --> 00:47:52.660
Anyway, that's a Kinsey tidbit for you.
总之，这就是给你们的金赛花絮。

1178
00:47:52.660 --> 00:47:58.560
So the end of this episode, Pam has been crying and Jim wants to cheer her up.
这一集的结尾，帕姆一直在哭，吉姆想让她振作起来。

1179
00:47:58.600 --> 00:48:02.040
So he puts Michael's world's best boss mug in Jell-O.
于是他把迈克尔的“世界最佳老板”马克杯放进了果冻里。

1180
00:48:02.260 --> 00:48:05.180
Now this was exclusive to our show.
这可是我们剧集的独创。

1181
00:48:05.340 --> 00:48:05.560
Yes.
没错。

1182
00:48:05.760 --> 00:48:06.780
So the whole-
所以整个……

1183
00:48:06.780 --> 00:48:07.760
It's not in the BBC version.
BBC版本里没有这个。

1184
00:48:07.760 --> 00:48:08.240
That's right.
没错。

1185
00:48:08.420 --> 00:48:12.580
The mug itself is set up in an early talking head.
马克杯本身在早期的采访镜头里就出现过。

1186
00:48:12.640 --> 00:48:19.520
And then this convention of ending the episode with Jim doing something sweet for Pam by putting the mug in Jell-O.
然后这种以吉姆为帕姆做点贴心事，把马克杯放进果冻里来结束这一集的设定。

1187
00:48:19.660 --> 00:48:21.920
That was all Greg Daniel's idea.
那全是格雷格·丹尼尔斯的主意。

1188
00:48:21.920 --> 00:48:24.560
And I think it's such a sweet way to end the show.
我觉得这是结束这一集非常温馨的方式。

1189
00:48:25.780 --> 00:48:27.000
And that's the last shot.
那是最后一个镜头。

1190
00:48:27.260 --> 00:48:28.200
Oh my God, Jenna.
天哪，珍娜。

1191
00:48:28.400 --> 00:48:28.680
That's it.
就这样。

1192
00:48:28.860 --> 00:48:29.660
We just did it.
我们刚刚完成了。

1193
00:48:29.760 --> 00:48:30.300
We did it.
我们做到了。

1194
00:48:30.420 --> 00:48:30.880
We did it.
我们做到了。

1195
00:48:30.920 --> 00:48:31.840
We were really nervous.
我们真的很紧张。

1196
00:48:31.840 --> 00:48:32.220
We did our first podcaSt.
我们完成了第一期播客。

1197
00:48:32.500 --> 00:48:34.920
You guys, we really, we were really nervous.
伙计们，我们真的，我们真的很紧张。

1198
00:48:35.060 --> 00:48:45.020
We actually, in the middle of doing this, I was getting so nervous that Angela made us turn off the microphones and have a dance party.
其实在录制过程中，我紧张得安吉拉不得不让我们关掉麦克风，跳了一场舞。

1199
00:48:45.100 --> 00:48:45.380
I did.
我确实这么做了。

1200
00:48:45.540 --> 00:48:46.360
To loosen me up.
为了让我放松下来。

1201
00:48:46.480 --> 00:48:46.800
I did.
我确实做了。

1202
00:48:46.840 --> 00:48:50.880
I put on Taylor Swift's paper rings and I made her dance around and get out of her head.
我放了泰勒·斯威夫特的《Paper Rings》，让她跳跳舞，放松一下心情。

1203
00:48:50.880 --> 00:48:51.700
I was spiraling.
我当时有点钻牛角尖了。

1204
00:48:51.920 --> 00:48:52.480
You were.
你确实是。

1205
00:48:52.600 --> 00:48:53.280
But here's the thing.
但重点是。

1206
00:48:53.380 --> 00:48:54.220
This is why we're nervous.
这就是我们紧张的原因。

1207
00:48:54.400 --> 00:48:57.440
It's because the show means so much to us.
因为这个节目对我们意义重大。

1208
00:48:57.500 --> 00:49:00.240
And we are new, obviously, to the podcast scene.
而且显然，我们是播客界的新人。

1209
00:49:00.420 --> 00:49:02.620
And your support has been overwhelming.
你们的支持让我们受宠若惊。

1210
00:49:02.820 --> 00:49:06.720
I literally teared up when we let you guys know we were doing a podcaSt.
当我们告诉大家我们要开播客时，我真的热泪盈眶。

1211
00:49:07.000 --> 00:49:11.420
And just the immediate support from all of you out there, I got a little emotional.
你们所有人给予的即时支持，让我有点情绪激动。

1212
00:49:11.600 --> 00:49:11.960
Me too.
我也是。

1213
00:49:11.960 --> 00:49:13.600
So I just thank you guys so much.
所以我真的非常感谢你们。

1214
00:49:13.760 --> 00:49:19.660
And just know how much it means to us that this show that is so special to us keeps finding an audience.
请一定要知道，这个对我们如此特别的节目能不断找到听众，对我们来说意义有多重大。

1215
00:49:19.660 --> 00:49:21.800
It just really means the world to us.
这真的对我们意义非凡。

1216
00:49:21.860 --> 00:49:23.560
It's changed our lives forever.
它永远改变了我们的生活。

1217
00:49:23.560 --> 00:49:24.120
Yeah.
是的。

1218
00:49:24.360 --> 00:49:24.620
Yeah.
没错。

1219
00:49:24.880 --> 00:49:25.760
So thank you.
所以谢谢你们。

1220
00:49:26.120 --> 00:49:27.000
Thank you, guys.
谢谢大家。

1221
00:49:27.320 --> 00:49:27.640
All right.
好了。

